{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md'","aggregated_output":"     1\t# \"Forecast unavailable\" for number questions: the design, ready for when release work opens\n     2\t\n     3\t**Status: design only. Nothing is built.** Alex decided the behaviour twice:\n     4\t- D726, \"同意\": until the number answers pass, a first release shows number questions with their sources and \"Forecast unavailable\",\n     5\t  with the band, the forecast text and its history withheld together; \"it is built with the release work, which is not started\";\n     6\t- D756, \"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线\".\n     7\t\n     8\tOpening release work is Alex's call (council 72). This page makes the build a known, reviewed slice for that moment.\n     9\t\n    10\t**Revision 3: one structural rule instead of a list of leaks.** Rounds 72 and 72b each found new paths by which a withheld forecast\n    11\tcould reach a reader:\n    12\t- the idea card;\n    13\t- the closing text;\n    14\t- an idea summary that re-reads the ladder;\n    15\t- a release page that reloads from the live POC service;\n    16\t- a translated export;\n    17\t- a Yes/No explanation that quotes a number question's band.\n    18\t\n    19\tA rule that withholds fields reader by reader will keep missing one (AGENTS §1: \"when one mechanism draws findings round after round,\n    20\tstop answering findings: propose one structural rule\"). Revision 3 replaces that rule with an allow-list at one boundary.\n    21\t\n    22\t## 1. The gap, measured at $0 (2026-11-23)\n    23\t\n    24\tThe stored poc-v118 store `poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/views.sqlite`, read-only, gives:\n    25\t- **The number question v8 (FY2027 Data Center revenue)** exposes its band, label, condition, reasons, 75 judgements and 69 change rows.\n    26\t- **Its idea input** reads \"Bullish … $350 billion to under $400 billion\".\n    27\t- **Yes/No explanations quote number forecasts:**\n    28\t  - `old-3` `v36`, judgement 799: \"around $1 trillion\" for 2027 spending;\n    29\t  - `old-1` `v10`, judgement 865: the selected bands of both spending questions.\n    30\t\n    31\t  The judge is shown related questions' selected bands (`views/judging.py:208`), and its prose can repeat them.\n    32\t\n    33\t## 2. The structural rule: one release export, allow-listed\n    34\t\n    35\t- **One exporter writes the release data:** `release_export`, a single function beside `service.py`. It emits only the fields on an\n    36\t  explicit allow-list. A field not on the list cannot appear, so a new or overlooked path fails closed.\n    37\t- **The release reads only that export.** Its page, its static build and its API, if any, read nothing else:\n    38\t  - no live POC service;\n    39\t  - no `/library` reload (`poc/ui/src/bootstrap.js` must not fetch in a release build);\n    40\t  - no prepared or translated JSON (`scripts/mock_translate.py`'s `data.en.json`);\n    41\t  - no `--composite-trials` input.\n    42\t\n    43\t  The static builder refuses any input not produced by `release_export`, which carries a marker and the allow-list version.\n    44\t- **For a number question, the allow-list is:**\n    45\t  - the question and its id;\n    46\t  - the evidence in force: one-line, quote, speaker, original day, tier and sources, amounts as quoted;\n    47\t  - the marker \"Forecast unavailable\".\n    48\t\n    49\t  Nothing else is listed:\n    50\t  - no ladder;\n    51\t  - no band, label or condition;\n    52\t  - no reasons or why_changed;\n    53\t  - no history, counts or assessment dates;\n    54\t  - no closing band (\"closed\" only);\n    55\t  - no theme pushes, no composite, no idea derived from its forecast.\n    56\t- **Ideas.** The release's idea composition (`idea.py`, `idea_composite.py`) runs on export data only. A number question enters it\n    57\t  as question and evidence with the marker. Its ladder is not read from storage in either the answer-format build or the summary\n    58\t  input (`idea_composite.py:255`, `:281`; `poc-v118-idea.json:94`). The test inspects the composed request itself, not only the\n    59\t  delivered card.\n    60\t- **The POC is unchanged.** Its API, MCP and page keep today's behaviour. Whether colleagues' POC page also changes is a separate\n    61\t  later choice for Alex.\n    62\t\n    63\t## 3. Identity: what a number question is (verified on four stores by council 72b)\n    64\t\n    65\tA view is a number question unless one of the following excludes it:\n    66\t1. **An event.** The view key's measure is in `identity.EVENT_MEASURES` (`event`, `policy_event`). That covers 85 of 85 event\n    67\t   questions in the three comparison stores.\n    68\t2. **A Yes/No question.** The ladder has exactly two labels which, canonicalised with the existing vocabulary\n    69\t   (`vocabulary.canonical`), are Yes and No in either order. The sealed ledger's 30 such questions use `是` and `否`. The Xbox `v37`\n    70\t   (`growth_rate`, bounds around zero) is Yes/No.\n    71\t\n    72\tEvery other view is a number question. Its forecast is withheld whether its bands come from `lo`/`hi`, parse from the conditions\n    73\t(the sealed `v3`), or cannot be resolved. An unresolved record is withheld and listed in the release check, with a key or without\n    74\t(council 72b: an `old-1/v8` copy without bounds does not parse, and its key still exists).\n    75\t\n    76\tCounts (council 72b), number / event or Yes/No:\n    77\t- `old-1` 19 / 28, `old-2` 17 / 26, `old-3` 18 / 31;\n    78\t- the sealed ledger: 43 parse as money, 21 are withheld as unresolved, 30 are Yes/No.\n    79\t\n    80\tNo wrong show-or-withhold result was found.\n    81\t\n    82\t## 4. Yes/No questions: an open choice for Alex (not decided here)\n    83\t\n    84\tD726 covers number questions. A Yes/No question's band is not a number forecast, but its stored explanation can quote one (§1). The\n    85\tallow-list must say which Yes/No fields the release shows:\n    86\t- **(a)** the question, its evidence and its answer (Yes/No and label), with no explanation text. Safe, and it removes the reasoning\n    87\t  readers would see.\n    88\t- **(b)** as (a), plus the explanation only for judgements whose request showed the judge no number question's state. Code can\n    89\t  decide this from the stored request (`views/judging.py`, which builds the related questions shown). It keeps the reasoning where it\n    90\t  cannot quote a number forecast.\n    91\t- **Claude's lean is (b).** It keeps value and is decided by structure. It needs a $0 census of how many Yes/No judgements it keeps\n    92\t  on the stored stores before release.\n    93\t\n    94\t## 5. Tests and the $0 release check (each names its row above)\n    95\t\n    96\t- **Fixtures (real store on a temporary path):**\n    97\t  - a number question with `lo`/`hi`;\n    98\t  - one with bounds only in its conditions;\n    99\t  - an unresolved one with a key;\n   100\t  - a Yes/No question with numeric bounds;\n   101\t  - an event question;\n   102\t  - a Yes/No judgement whose prose quotes a number band;\n   103\t  - a real closing switch;\n   104\t  - an idea.\n   105\t- **What the tests assert.** `release_export`'s output holds only allow-listed keys (a schema check that fails on any extra key). For\n   106\t  number questions it holds no band, ladder, reasons, history, date or closing band; Yes/No follows §4's choice. The static build\n   107\t  refuses foreign input, and a release page makes no network fetch.\n   108\t- **Mutants:**\n   109\t  - an extra field;\n   110\t  - a fetch left on;\n   111\t  - a ladder read in idea composition;\n   112\t  - the identity mis-sorting each fixture.\n   113\t\n   114\t  Each must fail.\n   115\t- **The $0 release check.**\n   116\t  - On `old-1/v8`, confirm the marker and the same sources in the page and in the export data.\n   117\t  - Exercise closure on a temporary copy with a real closing switch, after first confirming that the unrestricted response exposes the\n   118\t    final band there.\n   119\t  - Check ideas with a recorded or test transport, inspecting the composed request.\n   120\t  - Use `old-3/v36` and `old-1/v10` as the Yes/No prose cases.\n   121\t  - Use one unchanged event question as the control.\n   122\t\n   123\t## 6. Not in scope\n   124\t\n   125\t- The judging, opening and extraction pieces (frozen).\n   126\t- The closed v13s line.\n   127\t- Other open defects.\n   128\t- No prompt or pipeline change.\n   129\t- The POC's own behaviour.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'release|72c|forecast unavailable|D5[0-9][0-9]' docs/CURRENT_STATE.md | head -80\"","aggregated_output":"91:**Measurement correction (2026-11-05):** Alex clarified that a gold-worthy topic already in the supplied library should not open again; an absent worthy topic should open. The earlier simple-A claim of a \"missed\" new topic was not scored against that rule and is withdrawn as a correctness conclusion. In the actual experiment, a Kyber topic was shown and passing follows Alex's topic-level rule; whether its exact release question captures the shipping milestone remains unverified. The experimental pre-article snapshots differ from the replay's day-start snapshots; 9 of 10 inspected examples differ. The current uncommitted replay default does not build a cold-start library; committed main HEAD still uses the old seed and startup filing path. Historical lexical coverage has a confirmed unrelated-topic match. The frozen gold and past scores remain unchanged. Audit: `../hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-parallel-refinement/measurement-context-scrub-2026-11-05.zh.md`.\n93:**Simple new-question diagnostic (2026-11-05):** At Alex's direction, an isolated prompt returned new questions plus article evidence without asking for product database fields. Four previously seen real dev articles each ran once: three returned one candidate, one returned none, all four quotes matched their source, and the gold-listed GPU backstop amount question was not proposed. Whether that omission is a new-topic miss depends on whether the existing library covers the topic. Two other candidates require source and independent-significance review; the actual experimental snapshot already had a Kyber topic, so its pass follows Alex's topic-level rule; whether its exact release question captures the shipping milestone remains unverified. This is not a production or full-pipeline acceptance. Details: `../hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-parallel-refinement/simple-new-question-results.zh.md`.\n109:Alex decided in D369 to capture core and supporting evidence without a strict boundary and in D370 to remove the 22 preset starting questions and separate earnings-report import. The replay entry now defaults to `poc-v118` (D374), refuses old seeded ledgers and baseline configurations, and continues to read existing non-seeded questions; earnings releases remain normal source items. This change has local contract tests but has not passed end-to-end product acceptance. The frozen historical rulers and results remain unchanged.\n130:- **Nothing is live.** The two-week run of D563 finished on 2026-11-16 at 01:23 local (`poc/data/clean-carried-run-2026-11-16/`, draw\n131:  complete, ledger $3.476 of $6.00); its readings are recorded (D564, [result](research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/carried-run/RESULT.md));\n154:10. **A new-system store being written serves its first day in progress** (D573, D574; `docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/page-contract/LIVE-READ-DESIGN.md`, B):\n161:**Where the lean path stands (2026-11-15; D489 to D542).** Alex is not active (D509); D439 is in force: choices go to the\n164:D511 and D519; the lean path $8.34 in all). Every stretch below is closed; its full record is in the decision log and in\n169:  that matter ([sizing](research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/comparison/COMPARISON-SIZING.md), D517). **Production stays the default\n170:  and both systems stay (D518).** Alex's product choice on the company's financial figures stands (D505: evidence for related\n178:1. **The new system's delivery gap** (D506, D508, D513, D514): a kept fact that bears on a question by a step of reasoning may be\n182:   inconclusive ([result](research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/effect/EFFECT-TEST-RESULT.md), D511). Paused.\n183:2. **The judge, shared by both systems** (D519, D520): on a question that asks for an amount it names a band when nothing shown\n188:   ([result](research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/missing-input/MISSING-INPUT-RESULT.md), D530 to D532). What the product shows is\n190:3. **The old system's duplicate questions** (D520 to D523): three pairs in the fresh week; one second question was never compared\n193:4. **The old system's filing under the broader question** (D529 to D531): the data-center revenue question never received the\n197:5. **Where decisions and code part on dependencies** (D541, D542): `writing.write` drops an edge that would close a circle with a\n204:  ([result](research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/duplicates/D375-PROOF-RESULT.md), D526, D528); the eligible same-day cases of the\n205:  fresh week read (D529). A real measurement needs a new version of the reading request and a paid run; not opened.\n208:  [census](research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/dependency-selection/DEPENDENCY-SELECTION-CENSUS.md), D537). As the code stands\n210:  seven filing links ([proof](research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/dependency-selection/EDGE-PROOF-RESULT.md), D538). A design that\n212:  ([design](research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/dependency-selection/SEPARATION-DESIGN.md), D539 to D542): two proofs on stored\n217:- **D368 item 4, the reading direction for preset questions** (settled by Claude on Alex's delegation): not measured (D536); the\n221:**The choice is made by the council under D439 (D544, 2026-11-15): the work toward production carries forward on the new\n223:switched, deleted or deployed. It is not a finding that the new system's answers are better: the cold reflection (D543) found\n226:and D439's scope names its steps; it follows the product rule on financial figures he last confirmed (D505); the fresh week\n234:**Since the choice (D545 to D550, all under D439):**\n236:- **The fresh week's answer choices, read and traced (D545 to D547).** Of 21 attempts on seven questions, one agreed fault of\n242:- **The gates the new system must pass (D548), in order:** the answer-choice step on Alex's lines (D400), not passed; the\n245:  release, not written ([frame](research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/NEW-SYSTEM-FRAME.md)).\n246:- **The first blocker (D549):** the step declines some worthwhile questions. From the July refusal review, no general,\n249:**The one-week diagnostic of the answer choices is run and read (D550 to D554, 2026-11-15): not clean.** Nothing is live. The\n251:in flight; it was ended and continued from the library after article 120, D551, D552); only the topics and the answer choices\n252:were then run (the matching and the judge are recorded as not run, D553; they can be run later from the merged trace by a\n259:for what a topic tracks. Ledger $3.67 of the run's $3.95; paid calls under D439 about $22.10 of $40 (Claude's ceiling). D544's\n262:**Changed in the code (D552):** each call of the new system's first step waits at most 600 seconds on a silent connection\n272:**After the diagnostic (D555 to D558, all at $0):** the council refused a rule that would take the first-named figure as a\n281:**The core-problem council (D559, 2026-11-15; asked by Alex after the week's result, his words in the decision log), all at $0:** the product\n294:**The reflection council (D560, 2026-11-15, asked by Alex; his words in the decision log), all at $0:** the goal is a\n302:then D559's comparison. The role of the six answer-choice lines is put to him after the pilot. No gate, line or frozen piece\n305:**The small comparison ran on Alex's \"go\" (D561, D562; $0.43):** with the week of 09-22's library the first step re-opened none\n310:**Where it stands (2026-11-16; D563 to D567; Alex not active, D439 in force; about $26.07 of D439's $40 spent):**\n311:- **The two-week product-condition run (D563, D564):** read in five ways; gate 1 (Alex's six lines) is not met there either (7 or\n315:- **The judge naming a band where nothing sizes it (D519, D520):** closed for Alex with its record (D565, D566): the judge's own\n319:- **Integration (gate 5) moved twice:** the product's page reads the new system's store (D564); the new system's daily loop now\n320:  closes due questions with production's closing step, walks calendar days and owns its sequence (D567,\n322:  closing on a day without items was invisible at the next day's start (`src/hivemind/replay.py`, D566).\n323:- **Waiting on Alex (D560, unchanged):** his half hour on the pilot's cards\n325:  `~/.hivemind-keys/pilot-deck-1/`), then the six lines' role, then D559's wider question.\n327:- **Gate 1's reading repeated (D568, D569):** the same 39 sends read again from identical packets give the same line verdicts; line 2's\n329:- **The product page now reads the new system (D570 to D573):** the page shows D397's \"Not judged\" parts beside the answer; it reads the\n335:- **Serving while writing (D574):** no partial day leaks into the completed-day view; a freshly opened page now shows the served\n338:- **Alex's page (D575, D576):** `docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/DECISION-PAGE-2026-11-16.md`, six choices in order, checked\n339:  against the records. The live-service design is paused (D575). Stage B's control line cannot be exercised by re-sending the judge (D576).\n341:- **The unlisted parts (D576, D577):** the request never ties \"the topic's wording\" to a field. 12 failing attempts on 7 matters leave\n346:- **The unlisted-parts probe (D578 to D580):** negative under the rule fixed before the send. The changed written answers left no part\n350:- **The Idea planner (D580, D581):** a new-system three-choice event is shown to it as Yes and Still open. The design is parked as\n353:- **The hold lifted, arm A2 (D582, D583):** Alex's standing instruction to keep going outranks D581's hold. A2 adds D436's rule for a\n361:- **Arm A3 (D584):** A2 plus one closed-set sentence that removes, for an event only, an entry that merely restates one of its outcomes\n367:- **A3 and the edge (D585, D586):** A3 is negative under its fixed rule.\n371:- **A fresh comparison of A2 (D587 to D589):** no stored topic set is held out. So the frozen first step ran on the unread week of\n375:    so the comparison gives no verdict (D589).\n379:- **The fresh reading (D590):** the frozen step on 5 fresh topics misses lines 2, 3 and 5 and meets line 4. A2 is better or equal,\n381:- **The due-day mark's split (D590):** Codex first readers fail D on 133 company figures with code's day, Claude on none. A D-only\n385:- **Ruled-out rungs that catch a postponement (D591):** in 296 frozen-step event answers there are 37 company delays on deadline\n390:- **The final-answer test's control line (D592):** an unchanged re-send stays at 4 comparable controls of 8, and delivering three\n392:- **The live store's operating contract (D593):** version 9 is agreed after nine council rounds for a $0 proof build on test stores\n396:- **The live store's proof build (D594 to D597; nothing deployed, no service restarted):**\n402:  - **Slice 4b (D598, corrected in D599 and D600):** one writer per store by an operating-system lock, preflight's one locked copy, the\n407:**The live-store contract's proofs are all built at $0 on test stores (D594 to D603):**\n448:**The one next task: when release work opens, a $0 check of the reader's screen for number questions (D756).** On a stored number\n451:- **Alex closed the v13s judge line at its STOP** (D756: end the line, release with \"Forecast unavailable\"). Nothing from it enters the\n453:- **No release work is open yet.** No other task is queued on the number-answer line.\n458:recommendation: close the v13s judge line, and carry D726 into the first release, so number questions show sources and \"Forecast\n459:unavailable\". When release work opens, the first step is a $0 check of the reader's screen.\n838:- **D688's recommendation, answered by D689:** keep poc-v118 as production and pause the hybrid's release line. Questions on other\n842:**Earlier next task, closed by D676 and D677 (D665–D675): read the release comparison's six draws when they finish, with the council-reviewed tools**\n850:- **Result, 2026-11-19 (diagnostic, 5 draws; Alex stopped new-1).** The new system loses on the release comparison.\n856:  - **The goal loop is closed (D677, council).** The old system stays and no paid work continues. It reopens only if Alex reverses D505\n873:  5. `d400_code_check.py` and `step2_lines.py`: the hard checks and the release status.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72.md\nnl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72b.md'","aggregated_output":"     1\t1. **Scope. Keep tonight’s work to the read-only design review. Alex opens release work.** D756 settled what readers will see. D755 explicitly put the first screen check “when Alex opens release work,” and the current state still says release work is closed. An uncommitted build would start that work. Reviewing the design now fits Alex’s direction to prepare for production. [D726:11004](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11004) · [D750:11658](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11658) · [D755:11816](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11816) · [CURRENT_STATE.md:448](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/CURRENT_STATE.md:448)\n     2\t\n     3\t2. **Completeness. §4 misses several ways a reader can recover the forecast.** The clearest example is the idea card. On the design’s stored `v8`, I read the input used to compose that card. It says “Bullish” and gives a range of **$350 billion to under $400 billion**. Hiding the forecast on the question page would still leave it available to the idea summary. [idea.py:120](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/idea.py:120) · [idea.py:347](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/idea.py:347)\n     4\t\n     5\t   - **Idea cards and related questions.** Candidate briefs read the judgement directly. Related questions do the same. The mapping and summary calls can carry it into prose, and the browser can turn judgement history into a composite score and chart. This also matters when `/ideas` is asked to omit its bundles. Apply the release rule before composing the answer. [idea.py:137](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/idea.py:137) · [idea.py:156](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/idea.py:156) · [idea.py:278](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/idea.py:278) · [idea.py:379](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/idea.py:379) · [composite.js:29](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/ui/src/idea/composite.js:29)\n     6\t   - **Closed questions.** §4 explicitly keeps the open/closed records. Their reason can contain the final answer. Running the existing closing-reason function read-only on `v8` produced “at rung 2 Bullish.” History and bundles return that text, and the detail page displays it. The public record can say the question closed without disclosing where it finished. [design:46](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:46) · [pull.py:16](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/pull.py:16) · [service.py:280](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:280) · [bundle.py:112](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/bundle.py:112) · [thesis-detail.js:204](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/ui/src/components/thesis-detail.js:204)\n     7\t   - **Live and offline exports.** Name `/library`, `/thesis-bundles`, their MCP equivalents, the JSON export and the standalone HTML. The HTML builder accepts existing JSON and embeds it in the page. Already-prepared data can bypass both Python’s bundle builder and the JavaScript adapter. The release check must inspect the delivered data as well as the visible page. The separate timeline report and bet card also print judgements directly and should be identified as internal if excluded from release. [hivemind_api.py:205](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/hivemind_api.py:205) · [hivemind_mcp.py:96](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/hivemind_mcp.py:96) · [mock_data.py:31](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/mock_data.py:31) · [mock_build.py:27](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/mock_build.py:27) · [mock_build.py:61](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/mock_build.py:61) · [prepare-data.mjs:12](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/ui/prepare-data.mjs:12) · [report.py:42](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/report.py:42) · [card.py:20](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/agent/card.py:20)\n     8\t   - **Search and processing dates.** Server search can keep its ranking. Semantic search uses the possible outcomes, and its returned score measures relevance to the query. Neither uses the selected outcome. The browser library separately sorts by latest assessment date, and `record()` reads the last judgement’s day and round. Those are readers of assessment timing. Reporting zero rounds for a question with 75 would also give the reader a false fact. [search.py:46](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/search.py:46) · [search.py:275](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/search.py:275) · [library.js:32](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/ui/src/model/library.js:32) · [service.py:334](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:334) · [design:45](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:45)\n     9\t\n    10\t   **The proposed number-question rule fits the three comparison stores but fails on supported data.** I counted numeric bounds on 19/47, 17/43 and 18/49 questions in `old-1`, `old-2` and `old-3`. On the sealed ledger used by the service tests, Data Center revenue `v3` has no `lo` or `hi` columns at all. Yet `evaluate(v3, >= $300B)` returned `holds` and the judged $300–350B range. The reverse case also exists. Stored Xbox question `v37` has explicit **Yes/No** answers with numeric bounds around zero. The current opening check accepts a ladder with every bound null. Define identity by the kind of answer the question asks for, cover both stored examples, and specify what the release does when an older record is ambiguous. The existing helper for linking questions has a narrower, asset-only purpose. [tests/test_service.py:18](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_service.py:18) · [tests/test_service.py:119](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_service.py:119) · [stored Xbox ledger:20](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-10-25-english/data-manifest.md:20) · [extraction.py:493](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/extraction.py:493) · [links.py:144](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/links.py:144)\n    11\t\n    12\t3. **Faithfulness. Show the question, its sources and “Forecast unavailable.” Omit the ladder from the release answer.** The possible bands do not by themselves identify Hivemind’s choice. But Alex approved “只显示问题和来源,” and D756 says **only** those three things appear. That also settles the proposed counts and processing details on this screen. Preserve amounts quoted by sources. For `evaluate`, the unavailable verdict and removal of the judged fields are right. `claim_position` describes the caller’s amount, but repeated calls can reveal the hidden band boundaries. Omit it from the release response and give the idea card a dedicated unavailable display. Today it either falls through to a generic badge or formats a “Judged” line. [D726:10997](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10997) · [D756:11833](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11833) · [service.py:553](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:553) · [idea.js:136](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/ui/src/idea/idea.js:136)\n    13\t\n    14\t4. **Switch. Fix the release setting at `withheld`.** One launcher-level choice is reasonable where release and POC share code. Pass it through HTTP, MCP, idea composition and the static build. There is no open question about the release default. The separate decision Alex could take later is whether to change what colleagues see in the existing POC. Research already reads stores directly. [design:55](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:55) · [docker-compose.yml:9](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docker-compose.yml:9) · [docker-compose.yml:28](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docker-compose.yml:28) · [mock_build.py:20](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/mock_build.py:20)\n    15\t\n    16\t5. **Acceptance. The proposed page check does not prove the promised screen.** `verify-page.mjs` generates a fixture and selects `v3` or the first thesis. The current UI calls an empty history “Not assessed yet,” and its schema requires at least two rungs. When Alex opens release work, use the specified `v8` with its 75 judgements and 69 change rows. Open that exact question, verify the literal marker and the same sources, and inspect the response behind the page. Include the closed-question reason and idea card in that check, with a yes/no question as the unchanged control. [design:74](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:74) · [verify-page.mjs:11](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/ui/verify-page.mjs:11) · [thesis.schema.json:369](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/ui/src/model/thesis.schema.json:369) · [thesis-detail.js:184](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/ui/src/components/thesis-detail.js:184)\n    17\t\n    18\t**Verdict — not ready for release work.** The design would expose a forecast through the idea card and closing text, miss a known revenue question, and display more than Alex approved. Revise those contracts before implementation. This review was read-only and cost $0.     1\t1. **Revision 2 leaves a confirmed forecast leak through Yes/No answers.** In `old-3`, the August 25 explanation for a shipment question (`v36`, judgement 799) says that the 2027 spending forecast is “around $1 trillion.” In `old-1`, the August 28 explanation for the Firmus investment (`v10`, judgement 865) gives the selected band for **both** the 2026 and 2027 spending questions. I read both explanations through `service.history()`. The judge receives related questions’ selected bands and reasons, and history returns the resulting text. Revision 2 promises to return Yes/No records exactly as they are today. Those requirements conflict on stored data. Preserve the Yes/No outcome, and specify how release readers handle explanations that disclose another question’s forecast. Use these two records as acceptance cases. [Design:95](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:95) · [judging.py:208](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:208) · [service.py:263](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:263) · [bundle.py:120](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/bundle.py:120)\n     2\t\n     3\t2. **Identity works on the four stores if the Yes/No test uses the stored vocabulary.** I checked every question. The three comparison stores split into **19 number / 28 event**, **17 / 26**, and **18 / 31**. All 85 event questions have an `event` or `policy_event` measure. In the sealed ledger, 43 of 94 questions parse as money, 21 further number questions are safely withheld by the fallback, and 30 are Yes/No. All 30 use `是` and `否`. A literal English test would withhold all 30 incorrectly. Specify exactly two labels, canonicalized with the existing vocabulary, in either order. With that reading I found no wrong show-or-withhold result in the four stores. I also verified both round-72 counterexamples directly. Sealed revenue `v3` parses from its conditions. Xbox `v37` has the `growth_rate` measure and bounds around zero, but its two answers are explicitly Yes and No. [Design:30](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:30) · [identity.py:10](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/identity.py:10) · [vocabulary.py:24](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/vocabulary.py:24) · [test_service.py:90](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_service.py:90) · [test_service.py:119](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_service.py:119) · [Xbox store manifest:20](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-10-25-english/data-manifest.md:20)\n     4\t\n     5\t3. **The ambiguity rule still has a gap for a record with a key.** Section 2 limits its fallback to records with *no key*. The opening check accepts a ladder with every bound null. I cleared only the bounds on an in-memory copy of `old-1/v8` and ran its five original English conditions through the service parser. All five were refused. The `segment_revenue` key still exists, so this supported shape reaches no stated outcome. Withhold and list every unresolved record, whether or not it has a key. That closes the gap without extending the money parser to every language and unit. [Design:34](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:34) · [extraction.py:493](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/extraction.py:493) · [service.py:422](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:422) · [service.py:499](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:499)\n     6\t\n     7\t4. **The idea card has a second path that restores hidden bands.** Revision 2 covers candidate summaries, related questions, evaluation, and `/ideas` with either bundle setting. But the configured idea-summary version reads the ladder directly from storage when building its answer format, and the summary call adds it to the input again. I passed `v8` through that helper with its judgement removed. It added back “at least $400 billion” and “less than $250 billion.” Exclude withheld ladders from both reads and inspect the actual summary request in the test. A clean `judged` field alone does not establish that the idea prose is clean. [Design:69](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:69) · [poc-v118-idea.json:94](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/config/poc-v118-idea.json:94) · [idea.py:350](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/idea.py:350) · [idea_composite.py:255](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/idea_composite.py:255) · [idea_composite.py:281](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/idea_composite.py:281)\n     8\t\n     9\t5. **The approved screen, `claim_position`, search ranking, processing dates, closing text, and fixed setting are addressed in the design.** The question page keeps the question, its sources and “Forecast unavailable,” including amounts a source actually quoted. Evaluation returns only the marker. Assessment counts and dates are omitted, and a closing record can say “closed” without its final band. Search ranks possible outcomes without reading the selected one. The design also identifies the browser’s separate assessment-date sort and fixes the release setting at `withheld`. These provisions match Alex’s decision and the cited readers. [D756:11833](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11833) · [Design:46](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:46) · [Design:65](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:65) · [Design:81](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:81) · [search.py:275](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/search.py:275) · [library.js:32](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/ui/src/model/library.js:32) · [service.py:553](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:553)\n    10\t\n    11\t6. **The main exports are named, but a clean HTML file can reload unrestricted data.** The page opens its embedded snapshot, then automatically fetches `/library` from an API that defaults to `127.0.0.1:8788`. It replaces the snapshot after checking only that the response is a complete library. The idea page fetches its bundles from the same address. Since revision 2 explicitly leaves the existing POC setting open, a release HTML file opened beside that POC can show its forecasts. Bind the release page to the release service or have it refuse unrestricted responses. Apply the same content check to prepared JSON before embedding it. The static builder also embeds `--composite-trials` separately from the main dataset, and the translated `data.en.json` export retains judgement prose. Keep those inputs outside the release package unless checked. [Design:72](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:72) · [bootstrap.js:20](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/ui/src/bootstrap.js:20) · [bootstrap.js:193](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/ui/src/bootstrap.js:193) · [bootstrap.js:254](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/ui/src/bootstrap.js:254) · [mock_build.py:61](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/mock_build.py:61) · [mock_translate.py:114](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/mock_translate.py:114)\n    12\t\n    13\t7. **The acceptance check selects the right question, but cannot prove the closing case as written.** `old-1/v8` has 75 judgements, 69 rows marked changed, and 9 actual moves between bands. Its only stored switch is `open=1, reason=created`. Round 72 generated the closing sentence by calling the formatter. There is no closing sentence on this question for the release page to hide. Keep `v8` for the page and same-sources check. Exercise closure on a temporary copy with a real stored closing switch, and first verify that the unrestricted response exposes its final band. For the $0 idea check, use a recorded or test transport and inspect the composed request as well as the delivered card. [Design:109](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:109) · [pull.py:11](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/pull.py:11) · [service.py:280](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:280) · [service.py:356](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:356) · [idea.py:218](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/idea.py:218)\n    14\t\n    15\t**Verdict — not ready.** An unchanged Yes/No explanation already discloses a number forecast in the stored data. Revision 2 needs to resolve that conflict and close the idea, identity, and export gaps before Alex opens release work. This review was read-only and cost $0.","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'wc -lc docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md docs/CURRENT_STATE.md\ncat docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md'","aggregated_output":"     201   26537 docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md\n    1204  135465 docs/CURRENT_STATE.md\n    1405  162002 total\n# Core PRD for the next phase: filing must recognise indirect relations the way an analyst does\n\n> Status: in progress (opened 2026-11-04). Alex: \"你把这个写好成下一阶段核心PRD然后不要drift, 把所有需要的context 全部充分记录，每次开始前都需要revisit, 然后开始做\".\n> This page is the single source for this phase. In a conflict: Alex's words → `docs/DECISIONS.md` → this page → the other design documents. This page's\n> conclusions, evidence, constraints, measuring method and process are not rewritten to follow test results;\n> test results go into `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/log.md`, and changing this page first needs Alex's word.\n> Amended 2026-11-04 (Alex replied \"go\" to the proposed amendment; D360): §5.2 drops \"also file under the other party's question\" and puts two\n> sentences in its place, one on choosing and one on splitting; §6's decision rule is rewritten. How it came about:\n> `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/prd-amendment-proposal.md` and `log.md` rows 11–16.\n> 2026-11-05 (D368): translated into English on Alex's word (\"不，用英文吧\"); §4 corrected to name the frozen standard's version 5 and §5 given a status line, on his delegation (\"你要来帮我看到底做不做\").\n\n## 0. Checklist before every start (Alex: \"每次开始前都需要revisit\")\n\nBefore starting any step, finish these in order; if one cannot be done, do not start:\n\n1. Read §§1–8 of this page in full; read the last three rows of `log.md`, and confirm where the previous step stopped and why.\n2. Check against §3, \"not in scope\": what this step does is not in that table. If it is in the table, stop and take it to Alex.\n3. Check against §4, \"constraints\": this step changes nothing frozen; a change to the frozen extraction prompt is the one place §5 names, and Alex's\n   word for it is already given.\n4. If this step costs money: its predictions and stop conditions are written down and frozen as §7 says (with their sha256 recorded beside them); the\n   requests are rebuilt byte for byte as §6 says; the control is re-sent the same day.\n5. What goes to Alex: one conclusion, one recommendation, one test, after §7's rounds of review; no menu of options; in plain words (the opening of\n   AGENTS, \"Explain and answer as to a sixteen-year-old\").\n\n## 1. Goal (end to end)\n\nEach question's judgement must receive the facts that can change its answer; facts that no question receives, those that bear on no question, must\nnot be piled into some one question. What is measured is the final judgement (the frozen judgement ruler, reader B, at the window end 2026-07-14), not\nany one step's own score.\n\n## 2. The core blocker (proven)\n\n**The system uses a fact for a question only when the fact \"states exactly this question's own figure\". An analyst also reasons onward from a fact: the other party's figure in a deal, price and volume for a product's revenue, a product's variants for its launch, and so on. The filing step cannot do this; the judging step reasons onward once it has the facts.**\n\nThis one blocker has two faces (described earlier as \"two problems\"):\n\n- **The parking lot.** Filing does not recognise facts that bear on a question indirectly, so no question takes them; yet to be kept, a fact must\n  first be filed (D209, D264). So D273 added the fallback sentence, which parks them in NVIDIA's total-revenue question. Of the reports under the\n  total-revenue question, in the part the gold read, 32–39% are ones the standard does not keep, 31–44% are kept but used by none of the 22 questions,\n  and only 7–10% are what the gold actually uses to judge total revenue (three draws); 24–44% of the total-revenue question's judgement citations are\n  news about other companies or the whole market (Intel graphics-card retail prices, a gas-fired power plant in Taiwan).\n- **Narrow questions starve.** Questions that only indirect facts can answer do not receive them: the custom-chip question received none of Broadcom's\n  figures in any of the three draws, and judged \"below $40 billion\" in all three; the operating-margin and NVIDIA capital-spending questions received\n  nothing at all and were never judged.\n\n**Evidence:**\n\n| Evidence | Content | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| Filing recognises only \"its own figure\" | The model says \"Broadcom's AI chip revenue is not cloud providers' spending on custom chips\" and \"Google Cloud's backlog is not capital spending\"; on a neutral refiling (no question id named, the rule not shown), 23 of 42 facts that matter are still not filed | `probe-filing-account-d1.md`, `refile-no_fallback.json` |\n| The judgement reasons onward once it has the facts | The custom-chip question's request of 7-14, sent 3 times in each of the three draws: as it was, 9/9 \"below $40 billion\"; with the Broadcom, Trainium and other facts written in that draw's ledger added, 9/9 left the lowest rung (6 times $40–60 billion, 3 times $60–80 billion), reasoning as the two readers did (\"guidance $16 billion, about $64 billion annualised, less networking chips\") | `predictions-one-test.md`, `one-test-result.json`, `log.md` row 8 |\n| Where the parking lot came from | D273: with the fallback sentence added, the core items on the extraction ruler went 64 → 68; the extraction ruler does not look at which question a fact is filed under (AGENTS §7.1, \"What it does not measure\") | `docs/DECISIONS.md` D273 |\n| What the parking lot holds | The figures above; an independent reader on 12 random articles: of 25 misfilings as it was, 21 were parked in the revenue question; 8 and 5 with the fallback deleted | `sink_by_standard.py`, the independent reader's report (`log.md` row 8) |\n\nAll files above are in `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/` unless noted otherwise.\n\n## 3. Ruled out or secondary (outside this phase's scope, each recorded separately)\n\n| Matter | Conclusion | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| The argument card | Not built; its code is deleted (Alex: \"好，删掉卡片代码\") | `docs/research/2026-11-04-argument-record/log.md` rows 4–11 |\n| The arrows of the question graph | Really wired backwards: a seed question's arrow means \"supports\" (D208), while the judging code reads it as \"whose conclusion to read\" (PRD 06). As a result themes are judged only after the total-revenue question, so the total-revenue question reads the themes' conclusions of the previous day, and in draw 3 a chain of questions went wrong in turn. But it does not explain the misfiling (filing comes before judging), and the gold itself judges data-center revenue as \"total revenue × 92%\". A topic of its own; settled by D368 (item 4: the arrow means \"supports\"), its fix to be built and measured | `core-problem.md`, `review-core-codex.md` |\n| Code removes the total-revenue question's own figures | True (\"keep only the narrowest question\" takes a seed arrow for \"a narrower sub-question\"), but each draw it costs the total-revenue question only 0–2 of the facts it needs | `log.md` row 8 |\n| A filing re-check added at the end | Recovers some, and misfiles about as many (independent reader: about one misfiled for each one filed right); not the solution | The independent reader's report |\n| One general sentence, \"the other party's figure in a deal counts too\" | The custom-chip question gains, but it pulls Morgan Stanley's price for a Rubin rack from the Rubin revenue question to the capital-spending question, and leaves some facts with no home | `answers.json` (the two arms definition and definition_no_fallback), `measure-corrected.txt` |\n| Tightening D259's \"leeway\" | Alex's own decision; this phase does not overturn it | D259 |\n| Opening questions (the Ohio guarantee was not opened); the two readers' disagreement on the China-share question | Another class of problem, not in this phase | `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/diagnosis.md` §0 |\n| Model drift | With the same requests, today about half as many facts go into the total-revenue question as on 11-03; the cause is not proven. Compare only with a control re-sent the same day, never with the archive | `log.md` row 6 |\n\n## 4. Constraints (what must not move, and why)\n\n- **The frozen ruler** (AGENTS §7.1, D261, D262): the extraction standard, version 5 (the signed version 3 with D248's seven boundaries and D250's four\n  evidence boundaries and counting unit), golden-v5, the seed questions and the judgement gold; not a word changes; a disagreement is a gap in the\n  system (D263).\n- **The frozen extraction prompt** (D274): v74i (`poc-v108`) does not change by a word; what this phase changes is the one place that holds the filing\n  rule (the description of the `links` field), made into a new version with a new configuration and compared with v74i. Alex has given his word for this\n  work (2026-11-04: \"好你去解决问题\", \"开始做\"); making it the default needs his word again.\n- **Frozen opening and judging** (D354): this phase does not touch them.\n- **The standard's text** (in translation): §6, \"file under the narrowest open question; when no question takes it, record no home and drop it, and read\n  each one at evaluation\"; §5.1, \"makes the answer to some question more or less likely\", with four paths, \"demand, supply, competition, pricing\"; §5.3,\n  \"another company's matter is not kept when one cannot say which question about the covered company it moves through a path such as demand, supply,\n  competition or pricing\".\n- **Decisions**: D207 (one home per fact, the narrowest question), D209 (no home means dropped, each one read), D259 (leeway: a figure question takes\n  \"the demand, supply, competition and pricing that make it more or less likely\"; the total-revenue question taking more is an accepted cost, \"bounded by\n  the narrowest-question rule and the driver questions\"), D265 (code keeps only the narrowest), D273 (the fallback sentence), D355 (the two failed tests\n  of the previous filing topic).\n- **Prompt principles** (AGENTS §6): carry only the standard and add no new rule; a general hedge-fund analyst: every rule and example reads the same\n  for a bank, a drug maker, a retailer or a chip company, names neither NVIDIA nor its products or figures, and is not taken from a test article; a\n  classification is written as a closed set with two or three examples per class, replacing the abstract wording; quality is not fixed by lengthening\n  the prompt: remove as much as is added, or write down the reason.\n- **Code decides only \"is it the same thing\", never \"does it matter\"** (AGENTS §2).\n\n## 5. What to do\n\nStatus: the links-rule version that carried items 1–3 (v74l) failed its one test (§8 step 5); D361 keeps the fallback sentence, so item 3 is not carried out. The plan below is kept as written.\n\n1. **Replace the abstract sentence \"makes the answer more or less likely through demand, supply, competition or pricing\" with the few classes in which an analyst recognises an indirect relation, written as a closed set, each class with two or three examples from other industries** (AGENTS §6: one\n   abstract sentence is a coin flip on every send; examples replace it). A first draft of the classes (checked against the standard line by line at\n   design time; it holds only meanings the standard already has):\n   - The question's own figure: this question's figures, guidance, estimates and revisions (estimates for another period or another population follow\n     the existing rule).\n   - The other side of the same money: a seller's revenue from the buyers the question counts; those buyers' orders and backlog with these sellers.\n   - Price and volume: a product's price or shipments, for the question on that product's revenue.\n   - Variants and parts: a product's variants, alternatives, key parts and schedule changes, for the question on that product's launch.\n   - Demand, supply and competition moves with a number: customers' orders and capital-spending plans, suppliers' capacity and prices, competitors'\n     sales and share, for the question they affect.\n2. **State how to file a fact when two specific questions both bear on it** (the problem the `definition_no_fallback` arm exposed: Morgan Stanley's rack\n   price was filed under the buyers' capital-spending question, and the seller's Rubin revenue question lost it). One home per fact (D207): file it under\n   the question its figure measures most directly (for example, a hotel's room rate goes under its room-revenue question, not under the\n   travellers'-spending question; a parts maker's revenue from carmakers goes under the carmakers' parts-spending question, not under a rival parts\n   maker's share question); when one sentence gives a separate figure for each of two questions, write two items, each filed under its own question\n   (code stores two items that quote the same sentence as one record linked to both questions); never also file it under a broader question about the\n   same company (the failure of D355's test 2: the model filed it under an NVIDIA revenue question as well). The original draft's \"when the other\n   party's question is open … file it there as well\" conflicted with D207 and was deleted on 2026-11-04 with Alex's agreement (D360).\n3. **Delete the fallback sentence** and return to the standard's §6: when no question takes a fact, it is not filed; code drops it as \"no home\" and\n   records it (D209), and evaluation reads each one.\n4. Change only the one place that holds the filing rule; report its length in characters before and after, and write down the reason for any growth\n   (this time's reason: examples replace one abstract sentence).\n\n## 6. How to measure (the ruler does not move; the method does not change again)\n\n- **Requests**: rebuild each stored request byte for byte with the production code, changing only the one place that holds the filing rule; the\n  rebuilt request's archive id must equal the original's, or it is not sent (`resend_filing.py`, AGENTS §5). Never re-send the archive's copy whose\n  keys were sorted alphabetically.\n- **Articles**: development set = the 54 articles of `selection.json` (already read many times); held-out set = articles the extraction gold read and\n  the judgement gold uses that are not among those 54, drawn once before the test, with the list frozen and never changed afterwards. Both sets are\n  measured and reported apart.\n- **Control**: the unchanged requests re-sent 3 times the same day. No comparison with the archive (model drift).\n- **Each answer**: goes through the production code checks and filing first (including \"keep only the narrowest\" and \"no home means dropped\"), and is\n  counted after.\n- **What is counted** (`measure_filing.py`, with its matching rule fixed: items are matched on the distinct numbers and the proper nouns other than\n  NVIDIA in the source text; a source passage the system quotes that overlaps the gold's passage also counts as the same matter; \"optional\" counts as\n  optional; the citations in the body of the gold's answers are read):\n  - whether each fact that matters (one the gold uses to judge any question) reached the question that uses it, counted per fact, not per \"fact ×\n    question\";\n  - per question: the facts that matter that reached it and the new noise that appeared, counted by the decision rule below;\n  - the parking lot: how many facts the total-revenue question (v1, together with v22) takes in, and what they are;\n  - noise: how many of the sentences the standard does not keep are kept; per question, how noise is filed (links on facts the standard does not keep\n    or no question uses);\n  - how many core and supporting facts appear; the facts that matter that are dropped; how many questions each fact is filed under on average.\n  - Matching still has a small error (spot check: the new rule mismatches a few and misses a few); say so when reporting the numbers, and read the\n    ones that matter one by one.\n- **Decision rule** (rewritten on 2026-11-04 with Alex's agreement, D360. The original draft required \"every draw above the highest of the control's\n  three\" and the like, which the control itself fails when measured again, so it cannot tell good from bad. Script `decide.py`; written down and frozen\n  before each test; each draw's numbers and the totals are all reported):\n  - **Totals, with luck ruled out first**: each article's 6 answers from the new and the old arm are randomly reassigned between the two arms 4,000\n    times (with a fixed random seed); the new rule's difference counts as a real change only when fewer than 5% of the reassignments reach it.\n    - Development set: facts that matter reaching the question that uses them must rise; the count under the total-revenue questions (v1, v22) must\n      fall; sentences the standard does not keep must not rise; core facts must not fall.\n    - Held-out set: facts that matter reaching the question that uses them must not fall; sentences the standard does not keep must not rise; core\n      facts must not fall.\n  - **Per question, counted by code against the gold** (development and held-out sets together):\n    - A fact that matters which reaches the question at least two fewer times under the new rule than under the control counts as \"one fewer\" for that\n      question; in under the control all three times and under the new rule none of the three, it counts as \"lost outright\". A move to another question\n      that the gold also uses it for and that is no broader than the original (one home per fact, D207) does not count as fewer; a move to a broader\n      question counts. \"One more\" in the opposite direction offsets it.\n    - A noise sentence (not kept by the standard, or kept but used by no question) that the new rule files under the question at least twice while the\n      control never does counts as \"new noise\"; filed all three times, it counts as \"outright new noise\". The opposite direction offsets it.\n    - Any question with a net 3 fewer, a net 2 lost outright, a net 5 more new noise, or a net 3 more outright new noise fails. These thresholds are the\n      smallest values that keep \"misjudged when new and old are exactly the same\" within about one in ten; at the test, first compute the\n      misjudgement rate from the reassignments; if it is above one in ten, raise the threshold most prone to misjudgement by one step, then compare with\n      what was measured.\n  - **Smaller changes** (a question 2 fewer, two or three more noise) cannot be told from luck in three measurements: all are listed, given to a reader\n    who did not write the rule to read against the raw answers, and written into the report; they do not decide pass or fail.\n  Only when everything passes does it become a candidate; a candidate runs end to end three times on the 14-day window (extraction re-sent, matching and\n  judging run as usual, scored on the frozen judgement ruler), and that step needs Alex's word.\n\n## 7. Process (no drift)\n\n- **One recommendation and one test at a time** (AGENTS §7.3, Alex: \"就测试一种，一次\"): write the design first and put it through rounds of review (own\n  checks, Codex read-only, a reader who did not write it reading the raw records) until a round finds nothing serious; write down and freeze the\n  predictions and stop conditions; test once; if it does not match, stop and take it to Alex (D355: \"如果有什么不符合hypothesis 的地方你需要终止然后和我说我们重新评估\").\n- **A review's report is a lead**: each finding counts only once it is checked against the records (AGENTS §1).\n- **A prompt audit before any prompt change** (`.claude/skills/prompt-audit/SKILL.md`): check the whole request against the standard sentence by\n  sentence, in both directions.\n- **Every step goes into `log.md`**: what was done, what came of it, the files; mistakes and overturned results stay in it too.\n- **Do not repeat what was ruled out** (§3).\n\n## 8. Steps and where we are\n\n| # | Step | Output | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Design: the classes of indirect relation (a closed set + examples from other industries), how to file when a fact measures both sides, deleting the fallback; checked against the standard sentence by sentence; length before and after | `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/design-links.md` | Done (draft 3, v74l / poc-v115) |\n| 2 | Checks at no cost: a sample answer written by the new rule goes through every code check; the new rule's text goes through the prompt audit | Same as above | Done |\n| 3 | Review rounds (Codex, independent readers, own), until nothing serious remains | `review-links-*.md` | Done (Codex 7 rounds, independent readers 3 times; round 7 found nothing serious) |\n| 4 | Draw and freeze the held-out set; write down and freeze this test's predictions and decision rule | `heldout.json`, `predictions-links.md` | Done (sha256 recorded for both) |\n| 5 | Test once: development set + held-out set, the new rule and the same-day control 3 times each | `answers-links.json`, `log.md` | Done (2026-11-04): failed: facts that matter reaching the right question, development set +7 (p 0.26); every other condition passed |\n| 6 | If passed: to Alex, to decide whether to run three 14-day end-to-end draws; if failed: stop, to Alex | `design-links.md` §8 | Stopped, to Alex |\n| 7 | (D361, Alex: \"按照你的提以来，但是你一定是自己反思多轮之后才给出的行动\") Measure the ceiling first: hand the source passages the gold cites straight to the frozen judgement; the custom-chip, operating-margin and capital-spending questions judged 3 times each at the window end, the custom-chip question as it was 3 times as the control; the fallback sentence is not deleted for now | `reflection-v74l.md`, `oracle-design.md` | Done: operating margin grounded 3/3, capital spending 2/3, custom chips 0/3 (the gap is in interpretation); the next step waits for Alex |\n| 8 | (D362, Alex: \"你继续啊不要scope drift and strongly follow evidence of your discovery and learning\") Two small changes where facts are not delivered, one at a time: ① when a quote is rewritten, code matches it back to the source sentence (changing nothing the model sees; verified by replaying the archive); ② a figure question's description states which figures it is derived from by definition (first sent 3 times each on the article that motivated it) | `delivery-fixes.md` | Stopped: an independent check overturned the first change's code (it would take in wrong figures); the second failed its trial send (1/3). The root: the signed standard's §5.3 does not keep two key facts, treating them as \"a restatement of known facts\" (proposal 6, awaiting approval); to Alex |\n| 9 | **Historical; superseded by D370.** (D363, Alex: \"乙\") At coverage start, record each question's starting figure once from the company's latest earnings report; the daily path still takes no restatements: design, rounds of self-checks and independent checks, validated first on the archive in the simplest way | `baseline-design.md` | Validated on two questions: the frozen extraction does not read the report's tables (0/3); with each question reading the report once on its own, the operating-margin question read its starting figure 2/3 and the capital-spending question 3/3, and the judgement then judged right (2/3, 3/3), about 2.5 cents. All 22 questions tested once (2026-11-05, Alex: \"你充分验证\"; files chosen by code, a same-day control, about $0.43): v10 and v12 judged right 9/9 each; no question already judged right turned wrong; but 5 of the 53 figures read were other quantities (the Vera CPU question and the Blackwell and Rubin question took a larger or neighbouring revenue line), so it failed condition 3, written beforehand. The model itself pointed to the reading instructions' sentence \"write the lines it is computed from, or the line the report uses for it\"; stopped, to Alex. Alex: \"改\"; only this sentence was changed (\"write only the lines it is computed from, or the same quantity under another name; never a broader line or a line next to it\"), tried on 4 questions first, then tested on all 22 (about $0.36): all three conditions passed: v10 and v12 9/9 each, no question judged right turned wrong, and all 46 figures were the questions' own quantities. Checked after an independent reader's challenge: the new sentence made the reading miss the capital-spending line in 3 of 12 reads, and it had been tested only on the one May report; the fourth version (a line-by-line re-check after writing) removed too much and failed; after a census of every failure trace (Alex: \"我需要你深度看完所有失败trace给我准信\"), the third version with the repaired quote check was chosen (D365): 0 wrong figures on the held-out August report; built into the production system (poc-v116; the $0 checks and the tests all pass). The full acceptance, three 14-day draws (Alex: \"跑验收\"; a same-day control; about $4.79): all passed: operating margin and capital spending judged right 3/3 each (the control never judged them), 53 against 45 in total (of 57); for the China-share question, the only one two fewer, both readers found the starting figures did not lead it astray. Alex: \"都做\": poc-v116 became the default (D366); the code was committed and a PR opened |\n\n## 9. Alex's own words on this matter (in time order)\n\n- \"你这个单独开一个专题出来解决 … 是promot，是系统结构设计还是到底哪里有问题挂错一堆东西，机制是不是有问题（一定要挂吗？有没有可能是杂音\" (2026-11-03)\n- \"So if it's a customer problem or other companies that you think is relating NVIDIA and it's the wrong evidence, then what is the standard for it? … from a hedge fund analyst standpoint, are these even relevant? Do you think your ruler is wrong in this aspect?\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"你确定下你接下来要改进的量化目标，以及你要看到端到端我们的管线是要做什么的，不要乱硬优化，要看到目标\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"就测试一种，一次 … 能不能自己有个超级自信的定论和证据再给我提建议\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"这些只是类型题，你需要抽象拔高我们现在的核心问题和卡点。这个很重要这样改下去才是对的\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"你把这个写好成下一阶段核心PRD然后不要drift, 把所有需要的context 全部充分记录，每次开始前都需要revisit, 然后开始做\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"go\" (2026-11-04, on the proposed amendments to §5.2 and §6 and on this test)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
