on\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-07-22.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-08-07.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-07-29.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-07-05.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-08-20.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-07-13.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-07-25.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-08-16.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-07-09.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-09-17.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-09-01.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-07-08.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-09-16.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-08-17.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-07-24.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-08-01.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-07-12.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-08-21.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-07-04.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-07-28.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-09-20.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-07-11.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-08-22.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-07-07.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-09-19.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-08-18.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-09-03.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-09-15.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-08-14.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-07-27.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-08-02.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-07-31.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-07-30.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-08-03.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-07-26.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-08-15.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-09-14.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-09-02.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-08-19.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-07-06.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-09-18.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-08-23.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-07-10.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-08-28.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-09-05.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-09-13.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-08-12.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-07-21.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-08-04.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-07-17.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-09-09.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-08-24.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-07-01.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-08-08.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-08-09.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-08-25.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-07-16.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-09-08.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-08-05.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-07-20.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-08-13.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-09-12.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-09-04.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests/day-2026-08-29.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/replay.log\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/archive.sqlite\n     1\t\"\"\"The service's as-of reads on the sealed ledger (real data, read-only). Requirements: docs/poc/service.md\n     2\t\"Checks the new path must pass\": as_of never looks ahead (views, switches, judgements, evidence, sources,\n     3\trelationships); evaluate reads every money ladder as one partition or refuses; a corrupt record is refused.\n     4\t\n     5\tRun: python3 -m pytest tests/test_service.py -q\n     6\t\"\"\"\n     7\timport os\n     8\timport re\n     9\timport sys\n    10\t\n    11\timport pytest\n    12\t\n    13\tROOT = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))\n    14\tsys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(ROOT, 'src'))\n    15\tfrom hivemind import service  # noqa: E402\n    16\tfrom hivemind.views import store  # noqa: E402\n    17\t\n    18\tLEDGER = os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'data', 'sealed-2026-10-24-run3-through-0815', 'views.sqlite')\n    19\tINF = float('inf')\n    20\t\n    21\t\n    22\t@pytest.fixture(scope='module')\n    23\tdef ledger():\n    24\t    return service.open_ledger(LEDGER)\n    25\t\n    26\t\n    27\tdef test_default_as_of_is_the_last_completed_day(ledger):\n    28\t    assert service.default_as_of(ledger) == '2026-08-15'\n    29\t\n    30\t\n    31\tdef test_state_as_of_never_looks_ahead(ledger):\n    32\t    # v3 (data center revenue) moved from position 3 to 2 on 2026-05-20\n    33\t    before, after = service.view(ledger, 'v3', '2026-05-19'), service.view(ledger, 'v3', '2026-05-20')\n    34\t    assert before['state']['position'] == 3 and after['state']['position'] == 2\n    35\t    assert after['state']['previous_position'] == 3 and after['state']['since_day'] == '2026-05-20'\n    36\t    assert before['counts']['evidence'] < after['counts']['evidence']\n    37\t\n    38\t\n    39\tdef test_a_view_does_not_exist_before_its_opening_day(ledger):\n    40\t    opened = ledger.execute(\"select publication_day from processing_steps where sequence_no=(select created_seq from views where view_id='v16') limit 1\").fetchone()[0]\n    41\t    assert opened == '2026-07-24'\n    42\t    assert service.view(ledger, 'v16', '2026-07-23') is None\n    43\t    assert service.view(ledger, 'v16', '2026-07-24') is not None\n    44\t    assert 'v16' not in {v['view_id'] for v in service.views(ledger, 'NVDA', '2026-07-23')}\n    45\t\n    46\t\n    47\tdef test_frozen_views_are_closed_only_from_their_freeze_day(ledger):\n    48\t    assert service.view(ledger, 'v24', '2026-08-01')['open'] is True\n    49\t    assert service.view(ledger, 'v24', '2026-08-02')['open'] is False\n    50\t    assert 'v24' not in {v['view_id'] for v in service.views(ledger, 'NVDA', '2026-08-15')}\n    51\t    assert 'v24' in {v['view_id'] for v in service.views(ledger, 'NVDA', '2026-08-15', include_closed=True)}\n    52\t\n    53\t\n    54\tdef test_relationships_are_as_of_too(ledger):\n    55\t    # v94 (opened 2026-08-15) depends on v1; on 2026-02-25 v1 cannot yet have it as a dependant\n    56\t    assert 'v94' in service.view(ledger, 'v1', '2026-08-15')['dependants']\n    57\t    assert 'v94' not in service.view(ledger, 'v1', '2026-02-25')['dependants']\n    58\t    late = ledger.execute(\"\"\"with m as (select sequence_no, min(publication_day) d from processing_steps where sequence_no>0 group by 1)\n    59\t        select count(*) from dependencies dep join views v on v.view_id=dep.depends_on join m md on md.sequence_no=dep.seq join m mv on mv.sequence_no=v.created_seq where md.d > mv.d\"\"\").fetchone()[0]\n    60\t    assert late == 28          # the relationships that would leak without the filter (Codex's census)\n    61\t    for dep in service.view(ledger, 'v3', '2026-05-20')['dependencies']:\n    62\t        assert dep['since_day'] <= '2026-05-20'\n    63\t\n    64\t\n    65\tdef test_history_lists_the_change_with_its_cited_evidence(ledger):\n    66\t    h = service.history(ledger, 'v1', '2026-07-01', '2026-08-15')\n    67\t    moves = [(c['day'], c['moved_from'], c['position']) for c in h['changes']]\n    68\t    assert ('2026-07-26', 3, 4) in moves and ('2026-08-15', 4, 5) in moves\n    69\t    assert all(j['cited'] for j in h['changes'])\n    70\t    assert sum(b['evidence'] for b in h['arrivals'].values()) > 0\n    71\t\n    72\t\n    73\tdef test_evidence_excludes_replaced_guidance_after_the_replacement_day(ledger):\n    74\t    repl = ledger.execute('select r.old_evidence_id, r.new_evidence_id, r.seq, l.view_id from replacements r join evidence_links l on l.evidence_id=r.old_evidence_id limit 1').fetchone()\n    75\t    day = service.day_of_seq(ledger, repl['seq'])\n    76\t    before = {e['evidence_id'] for e in service.evidence(ledger, repl['view_id'], service.day_of_seq(ledger, repl['seq'] - 1) or '2026-05-19')}\n    77\t    after = {e['evidence_id'] for e in service.evidence(ledger, repl['view_id'], day)}\n    78\t    assert repl['old_evidence_id'] in before and repl['old_evidence_id'] not in after and repl['new_evidence_id'] in after\n    79\t\n    80\t\n    81\tdef test_changes_cite_evidence_with_only_the_sources_known_that_day(ledger):\n    82\t    # e3 under v4 gained outlets on 05-20 and 08-06; the 02-25 change must not show them\n    83\t    changed = [c for c in service.changes(ledger, '2026-02-24', '2026-02-25') if c['view_id'] == 'v4']\n    84\t    assert changed and any(e['evidence_id'] == 'e3' for e in changed[0]['cited'])\n    85\t    e3 = next(e for e in changed[0]['cited'] if e['evidence_id'] == 'e3')\n    86\t    assert all(s['publication_day'] <= '2026-02-25' for s in e3['sources']) and e3['outlets'] == len(e3['sources'])\n    87\t    assert ledger.execute(\"select count(*) from evidence_sources where evidence_id='e3'\").fetchone()[0] > e3['outlets']\n    88\t\n    89\t\n    90\tdef test_every_money_ladder_reads_as_one_partition_or_is_refused(ledger):\n    91\t    # a money ladder is one whose conditions name dollar amounts; decided by the text, not by the parser under test\n    92\t    money = re.compile(r'\\d\\s*(?:万亿|千亿|亿|万)?\\s*美元')\n    93\t    evaluable, refused, no_money = [], [], []\n    94\t    for (view_id,) in ledger.execute('select view_id from views'):\n    95\t        rungs = store.rungs_of(ledger, view_id)\n    96\t        if sum(1 for r in rungs if money.search(r['condition'])) < 3:\n    97\t            no_money.append(view_id)\n    98\t            continue\n    99\t        bands, problem = service.ladder_bands(rungs)\n   100\t        (evaluable if bands else refused).append((view_id, problem))\n   101\t    assert len(evaluable) == 43 and refused == [], refused\n   102\t    # the non-money ladders (percentages, gigawatts) read partially or not at all, and evaluate refuses them\n   103\t    for view_id in ('v32', 'v51', 'v52', 'v61', 'v81', 'v93'):\n   104\t        assert service.evaluate(ledger, view_id, '>=', 1)['evaluable'] is False\n   105\t    assert service.band('最终担保融资金额为0至不足1000亿美元') == (0.0, True, 1e11, False)\n   106\t    assert service.band('截至2026-12-31，筹集总额不低于5000亿美元且低于7500亿美元。') == (5e11, True, 7.5e11, False)   # the dateline is not the bound\n   107\t    assert service.band('不低于100亿美元，且低于200亿美元') == (1e10, True, 2e10, False)                              # a continued clause is\n   108\t    assert service.band('FY2027 OEM设备及大型数据中心收入不低于FY2026按披露占比计算的269.79亿美元、且低于400亿美元')[0] == 26979000000.0   # exact, not ...000.000004\n   109\t    assert service.ladder_bands([{'position': 1, 'condition': '低于100亿美元'}, {'position': 2, 'condition': '高于100亿美元'}])[0] is None   # nobody owns 100亿\n   110\t    assert service.band('FY2026 全年总费用不低于 1650 亿美元且不高于 1690 亿美元，处于公司指引区间') == (1.65e11, True, 1.69e11, True)\n   111\t    assert service.band('FY2027全年总收入为650亿美元至720亿美元（含两端）') == (6.5e10, True, 7.2e10, True)\n   112\t    assert service.band('FY2027全年总收入不低于FY2025的220亿美元、且低于FY2026的391亿美元') == (2.2e10, True, 3.91e10, False)\n   113\t    assert service.band('FY2026全年总收入大于或等于104亿美元（Q2收入26亿美元按四个季度年化）且小于124亿美元') == (1.04e10, True, 1.24e10, False)\n   114\t    assert service.band('达到9000亿美元及以上') == (9e11, True, INF, False)\n   115\t    assert service.band('园区总成本恰为5000亿美元') == (5e11, True, 5e11, True)\n   116\t    assert service.band('同比增长超过70%且不超过100%') is None\n   117\t\n   118\t\n   119\tdef test_evaluate_judges_the_claim_against_the_judged_band(ledger):\n   120\t    holds = service.evaluate(ledger, 'v3', '>=', 300e9)\n   121\t    assert holds['claim_position'] == 2 and holds['judged_position'] == 2 and holds['verdict'] == 'holds'\n   122\t    assert service.evaluate(ledger, 'v3', '>=', 325e9)['verdict'] == 'borderline'\n   123\t    assert service.evaluate(ledger, 'v3', '>=', 350e9)['verdict'] == 'not_yet'\n   124\t    assert service.evaluate(ledger, 'v3', '<', 350e9)['verdict'] == 'holds'\n   125\t    assert service.evaluate(ledger, 'v3', '=', 325e9)['verdict'] == 'borderline'        # a band does not establish equality\n   126\t    assert service.evaluate(ledger, 'v3', '>=', 300e9, '2026-05-19')['judged_position'] == 3\n   127\t    # Codex's two cases: a [0, 1000亿) band straddles 500亿; \"不高于 1690 亿\" puts 1690 亿 inside position 3\n   128\t    assert service.evaluate(ledger, 'v17', '>=', 50e9)['verdict'] == 'borderline'\n   129\t    v27 = service.evaluate(ledger, 'v27', '>=', 169e9)\n   130\t    assert v27['claim_position'] == 3 and v27['verdict'] == 'borderline'\n   131\t    # Codex's second pass: a boundary written as 269.79亿 is exactly 26,979,000,000 and belongs to position 3; v70's\n   132\t    # dateline does not hide its bound\n   133\t    v84 = service.evaluate(ledger, 'v84', '=', 26979000000)\n   134\t    assert v84['claim_position'] == 3 and v84['verdict'] == 'borderline'\n   135\t    v70 = service.evaluate(ledger, 'v70', '>=', 500e9)\n   136\t    assert v70['evaluable'] and v70['claim_position'] == 3 and v70['verdict'] in ('holds', 'borderline', 'not_yet')\n   137\t    assert service.evaluate(ledger, 'v7', '>=', 1e9)['evaluable'] is False      # a yes/no ladder has no amounts\n   138\t    assert service.evaluate(ledger, 'v51', '>=', 1)['evaluable'] is False       # a percentage ladder is refused, not guessed\n   139\t    with pytest.raises(ValueError):\n   140\t        service.evaluate(ledger, 'v3', '>', 300e9)\n   141\t\n   142\t\n   143\tdef test_record_and_changes_name_real_rounds(ledger):\n   144\t    rec = service.record(ledger, 'v3', '2026-08-15')['last_check']\n   145\t    assert rec['day'] == '2026-08-15' and rec['round'].startswith('day:') and rec['items_processed_that_day'] > 0\n   146\t    moved = [c for c in service.changes(ledger, '2026-07-25', '2026-07-26') if c['position_moved']]\n   147\t    assert any(c['view_id'] == 'v1' and c['from_position'] == 3 and c['to_position'] == 4 and c['cited'] for c in moved)\n   148\t    assert service.changes(ledger, '2026-08-15') == []\n   149\t\n   150\t\n   151\tdef test_a_corrupt_judgement_record_is_refused_not_read_as_empty():\n   152\t    with pytest.raises(service.LedgerError):\n   153\t        service._json('[broken')\n   154\t    assert service._json('') == [] and service._json('[\"e1\"]') == ['e1']\n16:Each folder holds `views.sqlite` (the ledger), `archive.sqlite` (every model and Jev call, request and answer), the run logs, and for the two D167 arms a week snapshot (`views.week.sqlite`, `archive.week.sqlite`) taken before August.\n31:`keyed-2026-10-25/` (the keyed-views rebuild, D155+), `sealed-2026-10-24-run3-*` (sealed ledgers with their own `SHA256SUMS`), `old-2026-10-23-run*`, `service/` (the service's idea archive, search index and timing runs), and the loose `views-2026-10-25-v1*.sqlite`, `archive.sqlite`, `views.sqlite` files at the top of `poc/data/`.\n35:The SQLite ledgers, archives and budget journals of the concurrency studies stay on disk, ignored by each report folder's `.gitignore`; the reports, summaries and per-trial results are in Git. Inputs and the recorded golden: `poc/reports/2026-10-25-full-day-canonical/` (current-code sequential fixture of July 27: `views.sqlite`, `archive.sqlite`) and `poc/reports/2026-10-25-full-day-parallel-r4/` (start-of-day `baseline.sqlite`, the day's `items.sqlite`, the golden `serial/views.sqlite`). The live study: `poc/reports/2026-10-26-e2e-parallel/live/` (`inputs/`, one folder per trial with `views.sqlite`, `archive.sqlite` and its `cross-replay/`, and `budget.sqlite`). The fifteen-day oracle study (D182): `poc/reports/2026-10-26-multi-day-oracle/` (`serial/`, `parallel-16/`, `parallel-16-mutant/`, each with `views.sqlite` and `archive.sqlite`), started from `poc/data/english-v23-jev-2026-10-25/views.week.sqlite`. Earlier studies: `2026-10-25-api-smoke`, `-ingestion-smoke`, `-ingestion-v11`, `-within-item-parallel`, `-full-day-parallel*`.\n41:Ledgers, each a folder with `views.sqlite`, `archive.sqlite`, `manifests/`, logs, scripts and a pid file: `english-v29-nvda-3m-2026-10-27` (poc-v29/v30, paused after 2026-08-24, 352 MB), `english-v32-nvda-3m-2026-10-27` (poc-v32, 119 items, paused), the week tests `english-v32-`, `-v33-`, `-v34-`, `-v34b-`, `-v34c-nvda-week-2026-10-27` (2026-07-01..07, D199–D204), and `english-v34-nvda-3m-2026-10-28` (the resume with poc-v34 and the D202–D204 writer). Scratch archives of the extraction arms: `poc/data/evidence-gate-2026-10-27/archive.sqlite` (every A/B send of rows 61–62); of the evidence-in-view A/B: `docs/research/2026-10-27-evidence-in-view/ab-archive.sqlite` (git-ignored). Step 3/4 measurements (rows 63–65): `poc/reports/2026-10-27-stage34-gold/` on the main checkout (arm1, arm2, fresh1, fresh2, jev-contradicts, the 47-replacement writer replay), 135 MB on disk. Costs: `poc/reports/2026-10-27-nvda-3m/cost-ledger.md`.\n54:The end-to-end arms of 2026-10-31 (`docs/research/2026-10-31-reference-context/`, D253; `e2e_compare.py` reads them) are the sixteen folders `poc/data/e2e-*`, about 260 MB on disk and out of Git: `e2e-v69-dev14-2026-10-31`, `-d2`, `-d3` (poc-v69, no seeds, the control), `e2e-v82-dev14-2026-10-31` (extraction v71, one draw), `e2e-v69-seed-d1..3` and `e2e-v69-seed2-d1..3` (seeds v1 under poc-v69), `e2e-v83-seed-d1..3` (poc-v83 with seeds v1, the current control) and `e2e-v83-seedv2-d1..3` (poc-v83 with seeds v2, stopped on day 1 by Jev HTTP 402 on 2026-10-31; resumed by `run_seedv2.sh`), each with `views.sqlite`, `archive.sqlite`, `replay.log` and `run.out`. Backup for the move to another machine: `~/hivemind-backups/run-move-2026-11-01.tar.gz` (93 MB, 316 files, SHA-256 `c8ff99bab6ca01f82e1fe0bd7510c91966b9298d8e22d4ad74036c2ea06d966a`), repository-relative paths holding `poc/data/items-nvda-2026-07-01-10-27.sqlite` (236 MB uncompressed, SHA-256 `57bc25441fea325b…`), the sixteen `e2e-*` folders and the `loop-2026-10-29/Y5-v65-d1..3` and `Y6-v66-d1..3` answer stores; what to do with it is in `docs/research/2026-10-31-reference-context/handoff-move-2026-11-01.md`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
