{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '10994,11011p;11826,11842p'\nrg -n 'def (adoption_schema|bind_adoption)|theses\\\\[|position|rungs' src/hivemind/idea_composite.py | tail -60\nnl -ba src/hivemind/service.py | sed -n '252,284p'\nnl -ba poc/ui/src/idea/idea.js | sed -n '130,158p'\"","aggregated_output":" 10994\t  - \"要不要开一个新的判官版本来试修法（相关的题合在一次里算，每个数字标明出处，程序检查算术和出处）？\" Options: 开，先做 0 元那一关\n 10995\t    (recommended: the format and checks designed and through the council, then the $0 gate on five stored cases, four gold controls and\n 10996\t    three planted errors; the paid gate asks Alex for its ceiling); 先不开.\n 10997\t  - \"第一版上线前的过渡：数字题只显示问题和来源，档位和预测文字写成'预测暂缺'，等通过检查再放出来。你同意这个做法吗？\" Options: 同意\n 10998\t    (recommended); 暂不定.\n 10999\t- **Alex's answers** (2026-11-22): \"开，先做 0 元那一关 (推荐)\"; \"同意 (推荐)\".\n 11000\t- **Decided (Alex):**\n 11001\t  - A new judge version is opened for the bounded test of D725: related number questions judged together, with labelled figures and\n 11002\t    code checks of identity and arithmetic. It is designed and reviewed at $0, then the $0 gate runs. The paid gate needs Alex's\n 11003\t    ceiling.\n 11004\t  - Until the number answers pass, a first release shows number questions with their sources and \"Forecast unavailable\": the band, the\n 11005\t    forecast text and its history withheld together. It is built with the release work, which is not started.\n 11006\t- poc-v118 stays the product.\n 11007\t\n 11008\t## D727 · 2026-11-22 · judging-v13's $0 gate: the design passed council (round 46e); gate runs 1–6 and council rounds 46f–46j; the gate is not yet passed; one choice goes to Alex\n 11009\t\n 11010\t- **Design:** `docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/DESIGN.md`, v1 to v9. Council rounds 46 to 46e reached READY FOR THE $0 GATE on v5.\n 11011\t  - **v3's structural rule:** code derives every relation it checks from the calculation graph and the passage text.\n 11826\t  - Options:\n 11827\t    - \"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线 (推荐)\": the council's consensus;\n 11828\t    - \"换更强的模型再小测一次\": a stronger model or higher effort, with a small paid probe and a cap Alex names;\n 11829\t    - \"先停，我想谈谈\".\n 11830\t- **Alex's answer** (2026-11-23): \"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线 (推荐)\".\n 11831\t- **Decided (Alex):**\n 11832\t  - The v13s judge line ends at its STOP. Nothing from it enters the product, and poc-v118 stays the product (D690).\n 11833\t  - The first release carries D726: number questions show the question and its sources with \"Forecast unavailable\", the band, the\n 11834\t    forecast text and the history withheld together.\n 11835\t  - The one next step, when release work opens, is a $0 check of the reader's screen on a stored number question that has a\n 11836\t    forecast and history: only the question, its sources and \"Forecast unavailable\" appear.\n 11837\t- **Kept for the record, not built:**\n 11838\t  - the D725 consistency finding (separate answers contradicted each other in 8 of 9 pairs, joint answers in none);\n 11839\t  - the open checker defects in `PAID-V13S-RESULT.md` §5;\n 11840\t  - the v13s request and harness in `docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/`.\n27:def disposition_schema(selected):\n28:    \"\"\"One required property per selected identity prevents missing, duplicate or foreign dispositions.\"\"\"\n42:def bind_dispositions(answer, selected, records, as_of):\n43:    errors = model.check_schema(answer, disposition_schema(selected))\n53:def disposition_prose(answer):\n59:    schema = disposition_schema(selected)\n76:    dispositions = {}\n84:        dispositions[ident] = value\n85:    plan = bind_dispositions({'summary': answer['summary'], 'composite': dispositions}, selected, records, as_of)\n96:        driver['required'] = ['raises_outcome_position' if key == 'raises_outcome_end' else key for key in driver['required']]\n98:        driver['properties']['raises_outcome_position'] = {'type': 'string', 'enum': [str(r['position']) for r in thesis['ladder']]}\n107:    first = {t['view_id']: str(t['ladder'][0]['position']) for t in theses}\n111:            position = entry.pop('raises_outcome_position')\n112:            entry['raises_outcome_end'] = 'first' if position == first[ident] else 'last'\n164:        'raises_outcome_position': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['1', '2', '3', '4', '5']},\n183:    dispositions = {}\n186:        if ident not in allowed or ident in dispositions:\n188:        dispositions[ident] = {'kind': 'driver', **{k: v for k, v in entry.items() if k != 'thesis_id'}}\n189:    converted = {**answer, 'composite': dispositions}\n190:    adopted = [s for s in selected if s['view_id'] in dispositions]\n191:    plan = bind_weighted(converted, adopted, records, as_of, [t for t in theses if t['view_id'] in dispositions])\n202:def adoption_schema(theses):\n204:    thesis's own endpoint positions, so the request cannot ask for an endpoint the binder refuses.\"\"\"\n205:    def item(thesis_id=None, positions=('1', '2', '3', '4', '5')):\n207:                'required': ['thesis_id', 'label', 'raises_outcome_position', 'reason', 'weight_percent', 'weight_reason'],\n210:                               'raises_outcome_position': {'type': 'string', 'enum': list(positions)},\n214:    choices = [item(t['view_id'], [str(rung['position']) for rung in t['ladder']]) for t in theses]\n222:def bind_adoption(answer, selected, records, as_of, theses, schema):\n231:    first = {t['view_id']: str(t['ladder'][0]['position']) for t in theses}\n242:        raises = 'first' if entry['raises_outcome_position'] == first[ident] else 'last'\n264:        return weighted_schema(theses), disposition_prose, lambda answer, *args: bind_weighted(answer, *args, theses)\n267:        return endpoint_schema(theses), disposition_prose, lambda answer, *args: bind_endpoints(answer, *args, theses)\n269:        return outcome_schema(selected), disposition_prose, bind_outcome\n271:        return disposition_schema(selected), disposition_prose, bind_dispositions\n281:        rungs = store.rungs_of(ledger, thesis['view_id'])\n283:            rungs = [rungs[0], rungs[-1]]\n284:        result.append({**thesis, 'ladder': [{key: rung[key] for key in ('position', 'label', 'condition')} for rung in rungs]})\n294:    \"\"\"Require one disposition per chosen thesis and bind identity/date metadata from trusted records.\"\"\"\n312:        raise model.SchemaError(f'composite: missing dispositions for {sorted(expected - seen)}')\n   252\t    return out\n   253\t\n   254\t\n   255\t# ---------- history\n   256\t\n   257\tdef history(conn, view_id, from_day=None, to_day=None):\n   258\t    to_day = resolve_range(conn, from_day, to_day)\n   259\t    from_day = from_day or '0000-00-00'\n   260\t    judgements = []\n   261\t    previous = None\n   262\t    for row in conn.execute('select * from judgements where view_id=? order by judgement_id', (view_id,)):\n   263\t        entry = {'day': row['publication_day'], 'seq': row['seq'], 'position': row['rung'], 'changed': bool(row['changed']), 'moved_from': previous if previous is not None and previous != row['rung'] else None,\n   264\t                 'why_changed': row['why_changed'], 'reasons': row['reasons'], 'cited': _unique(_json(row['cited_evidence_json'])), 'pushes': _json(row['pushes_json']),\n   265\t                 'theme_pushes': _json(row['theme_pushes_json'] if 'theme_pushes_json' in row.keys() else None), 'round': row['input_id']}\n   266\t        previous = row['rung']\n   267\t        if from_day <= row['publication_day'] <= to_day:\n   268\t            judgements.append(entry)\n   269\t    arrivals = {}\n   270\t    for link in conn.execute('select evidence_id, seq from evidence_links where view_id=?', (view_id,)):\n   271\t        day = day_of_seq(conn, link['seq'])\n   272\t        if day and from_day <= day <= to_day:\n   273\t            piece = store.evidence(conn, link['evidence_id'])\n   274\t            bucket = arrivals.setdefault(day, {'evidence': 0, 'facts': 0})\n   275\t            bucket['evidence'] += 1\n   276\t            bucket['facts'] += int(vocabulary.canonical('tier', piece['tier']) == TIER_FACT)\n   277\t    replacements = [{'day': day_of_seq(conn, r['seq']), 'old': r['old_evidence_id'], 'new': r['new_evidence_id'], 'said_day': r['said_day']}\n   278\t                    for r in conn.execute('select r.* from replacements r join evidence_links l on l.evidence_id=r.new_evidence_id where l.view_id=?', (view_id,))\n   279\t                    if day_of_seq(conn, r['seq']) and from_day <= day_of_seq(conn, r['seq']) <= to_day]\n   280\t    switches = [{'day': day_of_seq(conn, s['after_seq']), 'open': bool(s['open']), 'reason': s['reason']}\n   281\t                for s in conn.execute('select * from view_switches where view_id=? order by id', (view_id,)) if day_of_seq(conn, s['after_seq']) and from_day <= day_of_seq(conn, s['after_seq']) <= to_day]\n   282\t    return {'view_id': view_id, 'from_day': from_day, 'to_day': to_day, 'judgements': judgements,\n   283\t            'changes': [j for j in judgements if j['moved_from'] is not None], 'arrivals': dict(sorted(arrivals.items())),\n   284\t            'replacements': replacements, 'switches': switches}\n   130\t      line: 'No recorded view on anything in this idea.',\n   131\t      summary: '',\n   132\t    };\n   133\t  const chosen = card.reading?.chosen || [];\n   134\t  const summary = esc(card.reading.summary);\n   135\t  if (!chosen.length) return { badge: 'No thesis', cls: 'chip--line', line: '', summary };\n   136\t  const e = card.evaluation;\n   137\t  if (e && e.evaluable !== false && e.verdict && VERDICT[e.verdict]) {\n   138\t    const claim = `${e.comparator} ${fmtUsd(e.value_usd)}`;\n   139\t    const at = e.claim_position ? ` at ${scoreOf(e.claim_position)}` : '';\n   140\t    return {\n   141\t      badge: VERDICT[e.verdict],\n   142\t      cls: e.verdict === 'holds' ? 'chip--ink' : 'chip--line',\n   143\t      line: `Your claim <b>${esc(claim)}</b>${esc(at)} ${SEP} Judged <b>${esc(scoreOf(e.judged_position))}</b> ${esc(e.judged_label || '')}`,\n   144\t      summary,\n   145\t    };\n   146\t  }\n   147\t  return {\n   148\t    badge: `${chosen.length} ${chosen.length === 1 ? 'thesis' : 'theses'}`,\n   149\t    cls: 'chip--line',\n   150\t    line: '',\n   151\t    summary,\n   152\t  };\n   153\t}\n   154\t\n   155\t/** The card element the canvas leads with. `state` is one of pending, answered, failed. */\n   156\texport function ideaCard({\n   157\t  text,\n   158\t  state,\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'round 72|old-1|old-2|old-3' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/README.md docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md\nrg -n 'def open_ledger|request_sha256' src/hivemind/service.py\nnl -ba poc/data/sealed-2026-10-24-run3-through-0815/SHA256SUMS | head -20\nls -l poc/data/archive.sqlite\nrg -n 'run3-through-0815|poc/data/archive.sqlite' docs/poc/service.md docs/research/2026-10-2*/ --glob '*.md' | head -25\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'round 72|old-1|old-2|old-3' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/README.md docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md\nrg -n 'def open_ledger|request_sha256' src/hivemind/service.py\nnl -ba poc/data/sealed-2026-10-24-run3-through-0815/SHA256SUMS | head -20\nls -l poc/data/archive.sqlite\nrg -n 'run3-through-0815|poc/data/archive.sqlite' docs/poc/service.md docs/research/2026-10-2*/ --glob '*.md' | head -25\"","aggregated_output":"rg: docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/README.md: No such file or directory (os error 2)\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:24:The stored poc-v118 store `poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/views.sqlite`, read-only, gives:\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:28:  - `old-3` `v36`, judgement 799: \"around $1 trillion\" for 2027 spending;\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:29:  - `old-1` `v10`, judgement 865: the selected bands of both spending questions.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:74:(council 72b: an `old-1/v8` copy without bounds does not parse, and its key still exists).\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:77:- `old-1` 19 / 28, `old-2` 17 / 26, `old-3` 18 / 31;\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:116:  - On `old-1/v8`, confirm the marker and the same sources in the page and in the export data.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:120:  - Use `old-3/v36` and `old-1/v10` as the Yes/No prose cases.\n19:def open_ledger(path):\n     1\te67be3104ce3aa663a03d65dd5bfbc2fc432fe6bb67c0d0094a0aec09953ffb5  ./run3-to-0815.out\n     2\t99f895a5cfbd444fe8ddd857f5d2d9b3abc40f9c0bafce515a2d89b74fb10470  ./mappings.csv\n     3\t2229c5c421eb28ea0bdd2ecfabb83cd5cbaf43797c3a948a68cfdc5bc8a7fcc1  ./agent.sqlite\n     4\tcf56afe8c9976eed20144123ef4260863822ccb20850a4e1aeb894bc40df51d1  ./replay.log\n     5\tb22b7a057676bdc5db39daaf994c0f7cc2fb7e180b13e10c24a60b97ccca9f04  ./views.sqlite\n     6\t5499d7cd3c75b25ac0233c1d45ef0c291594bc6eb897b207a018971bef665499  ./views.sqlite.day0.sqlite\n     7\tf2dd92c9e77ab0fb09257a33b14eb0da7d5602ea47e1bbe425f2ddc49a501621  ./report/hindsight-key.csv\n     8\tb4133c322a51c5a2272f9b088257e9d375edd56842399582cb25cfdd624623f9  ./report/beliefs.md\n     9\t961d836d6b4f1bec959d66f5f26c10df85cfa79a2d5c710f6325e1246cb08d5a  ./report/cost.md\n    10\tfb3ea5d0444336ccde3dee2064403eda07602aa75a3bee028842e544c559e5a8  ./report/hindsight-reviewer.csv\n    11\t7f689b66af2a1b5aaca016fe7feb710eed966c5a62cb31360857b7efc44624f9  ./report/timeline.md\n    12\t6b81fc2fbf1a216506adc133b57754f57a1aa62818f1e31f12599ec7092dc0a0  ./report/limits.md\n    13\t97a878ce37628bd37fd06e7f729a82bfb6ec734d52f449903ced90d0ea04517f  ./report/events.md\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff  118923264 Oct 24 11:20 poc/data/archive.sqlite\ndocs/research/2026-10-24-service/codex-prompt-2.md:9:`poc/data/sealed-2026-10-24-run3-through-0815/views.sqlite` (read-only); the index `poc/data/search-index.sqlite`.\ndocs/research/2026-10-24-service/codex-prompt.md:20:- `tests/test_service.py`, `tests/test_search.py` — on the sealed ledger `poc/data/sealed-2026-10-24-run3-through-0815/views.sqlite`\ndocs/research/2026-10-24-hierarchy-poc/plan.md:15:- 读取同一份 `sealed-2026-10-24-run3-through-0815/views.sqlite` 和现有向量索引，记录文件指纹；源连接只读。\ndocs/research/2026-10-25-english/current-state.before-refresh.md:140:Alex then started the pipeline build the same evening (\"数据准备好了之后，你清洗干净就可以准备开始去建这个 POC 的管线\", \"尽量按照那个系统设计来……做简洁一点\"), with no cap on the number of views. The simplified execution plan is `docs/poc/pipeline-plan.md`; the code is `src/hivemind/` (config, model call with archive and replay cache, universe, dispatch, extraction with the five-block prompts, the append-only views database with trigram search, matching in two calls with code checks, writing, re-judging with citation checks, the decided part of pull mode, the day-by-day replay with the look-ahead guard and no-backdating rule), `scripts/replay.py`, `scripts/show_views.py`, `scripts/report.py`, `scripts/agent_day0.py`, and the stack-side harness `poc/agent/`. Model: OpenAI `gpt-6-luna` (the old system's; strict JSON schema; it refuses a temperature, so only `reasoning_effort` steers it), DeepSeek selectable. The first live bootstrap (NVDA's documents 2026-02-25..07-23, three runs while the prompts were fixed: Chinese output, fiscal-year notes so FY2027's due day is February 2027, the identity rule in matching) opened 10 views for about $1.5 a run; day 0 (2026-07-24, 53 items, $1.12) ran on top of it and the belief mapper placed 16 sentences on the day-0 snapshot. Alex then asked for a small-range test before the full window (\"你最好小范围的测试下\", 2026-10-23). The first week's run and a Codex read-only review of the code against the PRDs (`docs/research/2026-10-23-poc-pipeline/`, each finding's disposition in `disposition.md`) found defects that were counted and fixed the same night (sequence numbers shared within a day, dependants judged before their dependency's new conclusion, one piece of evidence stored twice when two destinations disagreed, a resumed round repeating completed steps, the second matching call failing open, block 5 carrying ladders and state, the memo exception applied to every individual author, the quarterly filter failing on Chinese, re-judging too slow when sequential); the table is in `docs/poc/pipeline-plan.md`. The first run's data is kept in `poc/data/old-2026-10-23-run1/`; run 2 (the bootstrap, then 2026-07-24..07-31 with the day-0 snapshot) is in progress, and Alex then asked for the run to stop at the end of August for a full look (\"你别全跑，到 8 月底先\"); it is running. The same night, after a trace of the two model-side findings (cross-outlet retellings judged as new evidence; run-to-run variance in which views open), the within-view search was fixed for Chinese, the matching prompt restated the PRD's repeat rule, the extraction prompt was rewritten as checkable rules (v2, measured stable), and DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash was compared and declined (D62). Alex chose to apply the v2 prompt at once; run 3 restarted from the bootstrap three times in a row (question wording, then a successor check that compared label text and threw away the Q1 call), and Alex stopped the pattern: no more fix-run iterations. `scripts/preflight.py` now replays every stored answer and matching record through the current checks and prompts before any paid run (AGENTS §5); its first census is in `docs/poc/pipeline-plan.md`. Run 3 (bootstrap clean, 10 views, 0 failures) replayed 2026-07-24..07-28 with per-item re-judging; Alex then cut re-judging to once a day and the window to 2026-08-15 (D63): those days are sealed, and the same database continued to 08-15 with the daily round and finished at 03:13 on 2026-10-24 with no failures: 536 items, 633 evidence, 58 new views (94 in all, 2 frozen on their due day), 419 judgements, 4 rung moves, 0 persona events, $26 for the run. Results sealed in `poc/data/sealed-2026-10-24-run3-through-0815/`, report files in `poc/reports/2026-10-24/`, the readout and the three choices for Alex in `docs/poc/pipeline-plan.md` (which views to open, the one judging misread, effort level). Alex then asked to trace every item (\"我们 trace 一下每一笔你怎么抽取观点，抽了什么，为什么抽失败或是杂音多\"): `scripts/trace_items.py` builds `poc/reports/2026-10-24/trace/index.html` from the sealed database, the archive and the corpus ($0): per item the routing, the model's raw answer with what the code dropped and why, every matching decision with the model's reason, what was written, the day's judging, and a rule-based diagnosis (空手 / 全被丢 / 杂音多 / 多为重复 / 正常); the item's text, the request as the model saw it and the raw answer are files next to it. Reading it, Alex asked for the corpus labels to be tightened before any rerun (\"扫描一次 tag 需要收紧的地方……先别帮我重跑\"): ten rules in `poc/corpus/scripts/assemble.py` (my census found three: Commerce Federal Register notices carry no object, certification and policy exhibits are 不算材料, an aggregator page's author is the byline's outlet; a Codex read-only review found seven more: peer themes only on results/reports/calls, the issuing agency as the official publisher, copies across kinds, the 8-K Item 2.02 body not the table of contents, 6-K covers, video pages not full, the newsroom results rule, plus author-table additions), each with controls in `poc/corpus/scripts/test_labels.py`, applied by `poc/corpus/scripts/relabel.py` to a copy of the frozen corpus as `poc/data/items-window-tags2-2026-10-24.sqlite` (routed items in the range 584 → 480; the frozen file and the sealed results untouched). The one disagreement (whether Commerce anti-dumping notices on Chinese goods belong to the 中美关税 theme) was settled on 2026-10-24 by Alex's thesis test: none of the 89 China notices touches the chip or server supply chain and no thesis cites them, so the rule stays (`docs/poc/pipeline-plan.md`). Open defect: the official harvest's file names collided (97 notices, 56 with another notice's body; naming fixed in `harvest_official.py`, re-fetch needed before the next corpus build). Census, review and dispositions: `docs/poc/pipeline-plan.md`, `docs/research/2026-10-24-corpus-tags/`. No rerun has been started. The front-end mock is now a generated page backed by the modular Thesis UI in `poc/ui/` (D130): a versioned JSON schema, one adapter for existing bundles, pure dated model selectors, and separate card, chart, evidence, select, disclosure, canvas and detail components. The 22-line `poc/mock/index.template.html` is only the page shell; `scripts/mock_build.py` validates the data and bundles the modules into the standalone `poc/mock/index.html`. Agreed UI decisions D64–D129 are preserved. Card-native hover titles are removed (D131). The Thesis detail drawer slides in and out over 280ms with a fading scrim; interrupted motion reverses, and teardown cancels it (D136). Seven browser checks cover both directions, focus return, reversal, data replacement and teardown; X, Escape and scrim closes are verified. Connector routing is now shared in `poc/ui/src/components/connectors.js` (D137). The stored 12-branch graph has no overlapping routes; 94 fan-out sizes pass geometry checks, and browser checks confirm attached endpoints for 4, 12 and 41 branches, including zoom and range redraw. Scratch mutations restoring the shared lane or unbounded ports fail those checks. The Idea card and graph are corrected under D138: a shared 40px header, no duplicate decomposition rows, all chosen theses directly connected to the Idea, and related theses attached to their supplied source. The stored three-part response contains eight chosen and five related theses; all 13 edges and 14 headers were checked in the browser, including empty/null replies and a range redraw. Both the first-only-root and wrong-related-parent mutations are rejected. All 19 UI tests and 32 Python tests pass. Components use scoped DOM ids and event cleanup and accept data/callbacks; they do not call a model. `src/hivemind/bundle.py` supplies stable assessment ids and event dates; `thesis_bundles` (MCP) and `GET /thesis-bundles?ids=...` expose the same complete read-only input. Data arrives through `fromBundles` or `fromIdeaResponse` and becomes the immutable `thesis-ui/1` contract. Invalid payloads are rejected before replacing the current screen. The preserved local Idea matching and number control live in `poc/ui/src/legacy/idea.js`; Idea product behavior and the live LLM overlay remain the next UI task, explicitly deferred by Alex. Integration and commands: `poc/ui/README.md`; design and tables: `docs/poc/thesis-ui.md`. Verification: 10 UI tests, three rejected date-related mutants, and the full 31-test Python suite pass; the HTTP and MCP bundle routes were exercised through their real transports without model calls. Browser checks cover two concurrent component instances, invalid updates, teardown/recreation, empty history, date selection, replay, type filtering and the retained visuals. The final JS bundle is about 174 KB; the 42-thesis demo validates in about 23 ms on this machine. In the evening Alex reset the POC's direction (D76): Hivemind is a database with a search engine on top, packaged as MCP and HTTP; the caller searches, chooses and arranges views itself. Built: `src/hivemind/service.py` (as-of reads: views, view, history, evidence, record, changes, evaluate), `src/hivemind/search.py` (embedding index over each view's own text in `poc/data/search-index.sqlite`, cosine + object and text boosts, lexical fallback), `scripts/hivemind_mcp.py` (9 tools, stdio), `scripts/hivemind_api.py` (127.0.0.1), `scripts/search_eval.py`, tests in `tests/` (21 passing on the sealed ledger, including the HTTP front started as a user starts it); design in `docs/poc/service.md`. Codex's read-only review (`docs/research/2026-10-24-service/`) found eight defects, all reproduced and fixed with a failing test each (dispositions in `disposition.md`): the threaded HTTP server crossing SQLite threads, relationships and cited sources leaking from after `as_of`, the band parser misreading 18 money ladders (rewritten), \"=\" misjudged, stale vectors ranked as semantic, the eval script's `none` and exit code, the embedding error echoing the response body. A second Codex pass on the fixes found six more (a float conversion moving v84's boundary, v70's dateline hiding its bound, `--lexical` still embedding, an empty vector counted as fresh, a boundary no band owns accepted, a failed batch reported as zero work), fixed the same way: all 43 money ladders of the sealed ledger now read as one partition each, the six non-money ladders are refused, and the ranking says `lexical` whenever any candidate lacks a usable current vector. Alex settled the uncovered idea (D91, \"没有观点就返回null\"): `search` answers `results: null` when the library holds no view on anything the idea names; a similarity cutoff was measured on 25 sentences first and rejected. Alex then set the next step (D112): the service in Docker, the FE calling luna through the endpoint, the user's thesis as the idea card. Built the same evening: `POST /ideas` (`src/hivemind/idea.py`: search → one luna call that chooses the views that bear on the idea with one line why each and a short reading → code evaluates a number the idea states → the chosen views in the FE's bundle shape, `src/hivemind/bundle.py`, the shaping `scripts/mock_data.py` now shares), a threaded HTTP front with per-request connections, MCP over streamable HTTP, `poc/config/poc-v3.json` (the `idea` setting), `Dockerfile` + `Dockerfile.mcp` + `docker-compose.yml`, `scripts/idea_eval.py`; design and tables in `docs/poc/idea-card.md`; 28 tests pass. Measured once on 20 ideas: 19 model calls, $0.099, median 3.4 s, the $300B example reads v3 ≥ 300e9 → holds, nonsense ideas get an empty choice, one idea null. Docker: both images run and answer GET and MCP, but a model call from inside a container cannot leave this machine while Clash Mi's TUN carries only the host's traffic (host networking is off in Docker Desktop); the service runs on the host at 127.0.0.1:8788 until Alex picks one of the two one-line fixes recorded in `docs/poc/service.md`. Not done here: wiring the FE to the route; the Thesis UI and its versioned bundle adapter are complete (D130), with additive ids and event dates in `src/hivemind/bundle.py`; the Idea front end remains the next UI slice; English for the views' own text in the card (the mock translated 42 views once; a cached translation layer is the next slice, cost measured first). Open: `tests/test_search.py::test_search_ranks_views_with_the_object_boost_and_as_of_filter` failed once in the first full run after the null rule landed and passed in four full runs and five fixed-seed runs since; that traceback was not kept, so the mechanism is untraced and the failure is not closed. Alex then asked for the idea route to be probed for retrieval gaps while Codex cleans the FE (D132): 49 realistic ideas through search and the model (`scripts/idea_probe.py`, `poc/eval/idea-probes-2026-10-24.json`) found four retrieval mechanisms, fixed with tests the same evening (Chinese text terms, aliases only from the universe's new `aliases` lists with product names, word-boundary matching, a 0.30 similarity floor under null); what still misses is the k = 10 limit on broad ideas and the ledger's lack of H20 / share views; the findings and four choices for Alex are in `docs/research/2026-10-24-idea-probes/findings.md`. The FE wiring waits for Codex's unified schema; `src/hivemind/bundle.py`, the two fronts and `poc/mock/` are Codex's to edit. When Codex finished (D130 verified: 10 node tests, 31 pytest), the Idea card was wired to the route in `poc/ui/src/idea/idea.js` (POST `/ideas` → `fromIdeaResponse` → the explicit graph described by D138; verdict and reading on the card; null and empty choices told apart) and verified in a real browser against the running service; the superseded local matcher `poc/ui/src/legacy/idea.js` was deleted at Alex's request. Deep-tested in the browser afterwards (nine cases: numbers in English and Chinese, eight theses, empty choice, null, a yes/no ladder, the service down, the detail panel's three tabs, the time axis and replay); three defects found and fixed: doubled score signs, the reading cut to one line, and the service's uncached sequence-to-day map (an idea now answers in 0.4–0.7 s instead of 4–5 s). Alex then set the flow (D134): the idea is read by an agent that calls Hivemind the way a fresh Luna with the MCP would. `POST /ideas` now gives luna the tools search / view / evaluate / finish and the recipe (`prompts/idea-v4.txt`: break the idea into two to four parts, search each, read what matters, map each part to every view that answers or moves it, evaluate a stated amount, finish); the turns go to OpenAI's Responses API with reasoning and no server state (`model.chat`), every turn archived; code runs the tools, admits only views the agent saw, evaluates the claim itself and drops a claim when the idea states no amount; the MCP front's instructions carry the same recipe; the Idea card lists the parts with their theses. Measured on the 49 probes: views mapped per idea median 2 / mean 2.43 (was 1 / 1.73), no idea without a view, 1.6 searches and 3.7 turns per idea, $0.011–0.041 per idea; one mapping error the model made ($300 share price against the revenue ladder) is recorded as a choice. 31 Python tests and 14 UI tests pass; the card was verified in the browser. Alex then asked for the context cost to be measured: the agent spent 27,000 input tokens per idea, a quarter of them a catalog re-sent every turn, for the same mapped count as one call; he asked for the obvious split (D135). `POST /ideas` now asks the model twice (call 1: typed parts and a dollar claim, given a 250-character object list; call 2: map each part to the candidates the service found) and the service does everything between: one search per part, the dependency graph from the first part's views (upstream and downstream, with judged positions), the claim's evaluation, the bundles. Measured on the 49 probes: 5 views mapped per idea median (agent 2, first version 1) plus 2.3 related from the graph, 2,704 input tokens per idea (agent 27,048), $0.56 for the run; the one error that survives every arm is the model reading a share price as revenue. The agent loop is gone from the service; the MCP front keeps the recipe with the object list. 32 Python tests and 14 UI tests pass; the card (parts with object, quantity and period; related theses on the canvas) was verified in the browser. Alex confirmed the route as the design and asked for tuning plans on speed, cost and stability; baselines (12 s, $0.012, direct view stable in 11 of 12 fresh samples, full mapped set 0.4–0.8 overlap) and the ordered plan are in `docs/poc/idea-card.md`; the tuning then ran as 13 recorded iterations the same night (`docs/poc/idea-tuning-log.md`; results against the targets in `docs/poc/idea-card.md`): kept are the tiers direct / driver / context with at most three drivers per part, the market-price guard, the English re-ask, reasoning effort none, the service's second (canonical) query per part, one embeddings round trip for all of a part's queries (five of fourteen seconds were serial embedding calls), and the direct pick made among the model's own direct views (the earlier object-and-year rule had overridden a right label in 4 of 31 picks and judged 3 of 13 claims against the wrong view: TSMC capex against TSMC revenue, Meta capex against total expenses, Rubin revenue against total revenue); refuted are the provider's `seed` (accepted, not deterministic) and the canonical query as the steadier top hit (the model's query is). Measured on the final code, serial, 8 fresh ideas: 8.6 s and $0.0070 per idea with the lean mapping contract (no per-part reason, each candidate written once), 10.9 s and $0.0098 with the full one, from 20.4 s and $0.013; the first part's direct view agrees in 8 of 8 fresh samples (full) / 7 of 8 (lean); the canvas set overlaps 0.65 (full) / 0.55 (lean) between samples against a target of 0.8, the variance left being call 1's number of parts and secondary objects; zero price claims, zero claims against a wrong view, both Chinese slips caught. Two mistakes are recorded in the log (a replay that was not byte-identical cost $0.18; the pick rule itself). Arm E (no per-part reason, full briefs) measured last: first view 7 of 8, overlap 0.50, so the reason the page never shows is what steadies the mapping; the API and the scripts now default to the full contract at reasoning none (`poc/config/poc-v9.json`). Alex chose the full contract (D145, \"用完整版吧\"); the lean ones stay as measured arms. The gold set is written and sealed (D146, twenty ideas judged as an analyst, `poc/eval/gold/idea-gold-2026-10-25.json`, scored by `scripts/idea_gold.py`): the kept configuration gets the direct view right for 18 of 20, shows a trap for 2, reaches 65% of the wanted drivers, 22% canvas noise, claims 20 of 20. Alex then asked for stability to be improved without overfitting: the variance was decomposed at $0 (which secondary objects call 1 names 0.75, the candidates for the same object 0.78, call 2's driver choice on the same candidates 0.78; the canvas 0.65), a held-out set of eight ideas on other objects was sealed before any arm (`poc/eval/idea-heldout-2026-10-25.json`; the kept configuration measures 0.68 there, first view 8 of 8), and two arms were measured and refuted on both sets (candidates ranked by the idea text: 0.67 but gold direct 17 → 15; a clause per driver: 0.51 and 0.62 against 0.65 and 0.68). Rules after call 2 were measured at $0: two drivers per part instead of three gives 0.67 / 0.76 at gold driver recall 0.65 → 0.56 (offered as a switch, not applied); a second mapping call with drivers both name gives 0.73 simulated at a second call's price (in reserve). The canvas rule stays as it is; the next stability gain is upstream (one view per quantity, graph links between company and theme views). Before the NVDA rerun (D151): both sessions' work is merged in commit 7033c87; the five pre-rerun items were verified on the sealed run and two prompt rules corrected and proven on stored requests (role-v3: no product-trivia views, the H200 licence view opens; judging-v2: missing confirmation is not the lowest rung), configured as `poc/config/poc-v14.json` on the relabelled corpus; grouping stays out of the default pipeline; the English migration (137 Chinese literals in code, 13 KB prompts, the ladder parser) is Alex's call. A one-week run with poc-v14 is running (bootstrap 15 views incl. the H200 licence view, no product trivia; day one 48 items, 3 new views; a duplicate Rubin-shipment view by fiscal/calendar wording found). Alex then asked for a structural review (`docs/research/2026-10-25-structural-review.md`): the recurring problems share one root, identity and importance decided by the model over free text at five points, on a document-driven pipeline; he approved the correction (D153): a keyed view record owned by code, research subjects as universe objects with aliases, an analyst's watch list per object as the opening gate, model choices only among shown names. The plan with its tables and six small quantified tests is `docs/poc/keyed-views-plan.md`; results go to `docs/poc/pipeline-tuning-log.md`. Overnight (Alex asleep, D153): the week run finished as the baseline T0 (324 items, 47 views, 1 trivia view, three duplicate families, $9.57); the keyed contract was built into the pipeline as poc-v15 (D154) and iterated on the twenty bootstrap documents through T1–T2d until 11 views, 0 duplicate keys, 0 trivia; T4–T4c (the same week on the keyed library) found and fixed two more rules (a model-written scope is wording, not identity; the object is part of the key) and ended at 40 views, 0 trivia, 0 duplicate keys, a visible review pool of 23, −19% cost; the one cluster still split (OpenAI/Ohio financing, 8 views) is a watch-list gap to fill in the full rerun (`docs/poc/pipeline-tuning-log.md`, 今晚的收敛). Next, for Alex's go: the full-window rerun on poc-v15 with the watch-list additions (Meta total expenses, OpenAI–NVIDIA financing and Ohio campus capacity with aliases, SK factory capacity, operating_income in the measure list), then T5 (idea route by key lookup, gold re-mapped by key), grouping as universe subjects, the English migration. After it: Alex's word on the two-driver cap (steadier canvas, fewer of the analyst's drivers) and on a stable mode with a second call; then the two gold misses (an event view standing in for a quantity; a capex part invented for a tariff thesis) traced on the gold, and the cost arms (the reason capped at twelve words with the neutral example sentence, six candidates per part) toward the $0.005 target; the 6 s target is below the floor of two serial calls on this network and is reported as such, not pursued. The four example theses find an accepted view in their top 3 (`scripts/search_eval.py` exits 1 otherwise). The web mock still carries its own embedded data and lexical matching; turning it into a client of the API is the next slice and belongs to whoever is editing `poc/mock/` (a parallel session recorded D64–D75 there on the same afternoon). Nothing in the frozen design changed; the POC departs from it only where `docs/poc/pipeline-plan.md` says so. Then pull\ndocs/research/2026-10-25-retrieval-poc/codex-report.md:12:| S | [Sealed Chinese](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/sealed-2026-10-24-run3-through-0815/views.sqlite) | August 15 | 584 | 94 | 827 | 315 |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
